{
  "wireMagic": "pb3",
  "pens": [ {
  
  } ],
  "wsWinStyles": [ {
  
  } ],
  "wpWinPositions": [ {
  
  } ],
  "events": [ {
    "tStartMs": 120,
    "dDurationMs": 2460,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- There is a prequel\nto the \"Da Vinci Code\"."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2580,
    "dDurationMs": 2190,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It's called \"Angels and Demons\"."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 4770,
    "dDurationMs": 2820,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And in it, terrorists\nsteal one eighth of a gram"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 7590,
    "dDurationMs": 4050,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of antimatter from CERN to\ntry to blow up the Vatican."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 11640,
    "dDurationMs": 3060,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Because the thing is, when\nantimatter and matter meet,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 14700,
    "dDurationMs": 2905,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "they annihilate, turning nearly 100%"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 17605,
    "dDurationMs": 3335,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of their combined mass into pure energy."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 20940,
    "dDurationMs": 2850,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This is via E equals mc squared."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 23790,
    "dDurationMs": 3363,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It is the most violent\nprocess physics allows."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 28110,
    "dDurationMs": 833,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Let's go!"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 29880,
    "dDurationMs": 2700,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- Oh my God.\n(dramatic music)"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 32580,
    "dDurationMs": 1860,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- Now, that was just a novel."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 34440,
    "dDurationMs": 3540,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But CERN actually is making antimatter."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 37980,
    "dDurationMs": 5000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And we got to visit it. This\nis CERN's antimatter factory."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 43800,
    "dDurationMs": 1410,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "There's antiprotons..."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 45210,
    "dDurationMs": 1414,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- Yes.\n- Going beneath our feet."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 46624,
    "dDurationMs": 1736,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- They are under our feet at this time."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 48360,
    "dDurationMs": 4470,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- Here, protons are\naccelerated up to 99.93%"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 52830,
    "dDurationMs": 3312,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the speed of light and\nsmashed into an iridium target"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 56142,
    "dDurationMs": 4448,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to produce 20 million\nantiprotons every minute."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 60590,
    "dDurationMs": 4060,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This is so much bigger than I\nwas thinking. This is crazy."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 64650,
    "dDurationMs": 3277,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Antimatter is the most expensive\nsubstance in the universe."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 67927,
    "dDurationMs": 1643,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "$1 billion per gram."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 69570,
    "dDurationMs": 840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- No way."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 70410,
    "dDurationMs": 2910,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Go up. You're missing zeros here."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 73320,
    "dDurationMs": 1693,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- And CERN makes it to do something"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 75013,
    "dDurationMs": 1997,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that seems impossible."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 77010,
    "dDurationMs": 1470,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So you're making antiatoms?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 78480,
    "dDurationMs": 1260,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- Yes."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 79740,
    "dDurationMs": 2520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- CERN made the first\nantihydrogen atoms back"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 82260,
    "dDurationMs": 3667,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "in 1995, but they quickly\nran into a problem"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 85927,
    "dDurationMs": 4123,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "because those antiatoms only\nsurvived for 40 billionths"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 90050,
    "dDurationMs": 1990,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of a second before annihilating,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 92040,
    "dDurationMs": 3300,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "which is way too short to\ndo anything useful with it."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 95340,
    "dDurationMs": 3150,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "If only they could figure\nout how to store antimatter,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 98490,
    "dDurationMs": 2490,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "then they could study\nit and try to find ways"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 100980,
    "dDurationMs": 2400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "in which it might differ\nfrom normal matter."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 103380,
    "dDurationMs": 2844,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "They knew that any unexpected\ndifference could reveal"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 106224,
    "dDurationMs": 2256,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "entirely new physics."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 108480,
    "dDurationMs": 4383,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So how do you store antimatter\nin a world full of matter?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 113730,
    "dDurationMs": 2100,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Well, that's one of the problems CERN"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 115830,
    "dDurationMs": 3780,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "has been obsessing over\nfor the last 30 plus years."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 119610,
    "dDurationMs": 3210,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It has allowed them to do\nsome of the most precise tests"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 122820,
    "dDurationMs": 1710,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of antimatter to date,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 124530,
    "dDurationMs": 3003,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and they even managed to\ntrap antimatter in a box,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 127533,
    "dDurationMs": 3357,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "load it onto a truck and ship it."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 130890,
    "dDurationMs": 3270,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And they are doing all of\nthis to try and solve one"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 134160,
    "dDurationMs": 4350,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of the biggest unsolved\nmysteries in all of physics."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 138510,
    "dDurationMs": 1920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "To understand it, we must go back"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 140430,
    "dDurationMs": 3033,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to a discovery made around 100 years ago."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 145770,
    "dDurationMs": 2070,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Previously on \"Veritasium,\" we learned"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 147840,
    "dDurationMs": 2220,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "how a strange physicist, Paul Dirac,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 150060,
    "dDurationMs": 2820,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "came up with an equation\nto unite special relativity"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 152880,
    "dDurationMs": 1470,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "with quantum mechanics."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 154350,
    "dDurationMs": 1800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It worked surprisingly well,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 156150,
    "dDurationMs": 2490,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but Dirac was stumped by his own equation,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 158640,
    "dDurationMs": 2370,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "because the solution\nfor an electron at rest"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 161010,
    "dDurationMs": 1320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "was kind of strange."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 162330,
    "dDurationMs": 2100,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "There were two possible energies,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 164430,
    "dDurationMs": 4800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "E equals mc squared and E\nequals minus mc squared."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 169230,
    "dDurationMs": 2790,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But how could an electron\nhave negative energy?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 172020,
    "dDurationMs": 3600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Well, instead of throwing away\nhis negative energy solution,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 175620,
    "dDurationMs": 2970,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Dirac ended up proposing\nsomething radical."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 178590,
    "dDurationMs": 1543,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This negative energy solution corresponded"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 180133,
    "dDurationMs": 4907,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to an entirely new particle,\nunknown to physics at the time."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 185040,
    "dDurationMs": 2370,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It would have the same\nmass as an electron,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 187410,
    "dDurationMs": 2040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but carry opposite charge."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 189450,
    "dDurationMs": 3840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It would be an antielectron, or positron."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 193290,
    "dDurationMs": 1890,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Miraculously, a year later,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 195180,
    "dDurationMs": 4140,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the first positron was\nobserved by accident in nature."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 199320,
    "dDurationMs": 1590,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Over the following decades,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 200910,
    "dDurationMs": 3120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "physicists built on\nDirac's equation to form"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 204030,
    "dDurationMs": 1920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "an entirely new framework"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 205950,
    "dDurationMs": 3060,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of quantum mechanics,\nquantum field theory."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 209010,
    "dDurationMs": 1950,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- This didn't just explain why there"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 210960,
    "dDurationMs": 2222,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "are antiparticles, but it also answered"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 213182,
    "dDurationMs": 2576,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "a more fundamental question, which is,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 215758,
    "dDurationMs": 5000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "why is every electron in the\nuniverse exactly the same?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 220770,
    "dDurationMs": 2970,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The answer began to take\nshape when people figured out"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 223740,
    "dDurationMs": 2610,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that fundamental particles\naren't just particles"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 226350,
    "dDurationMs": 3930,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "or waves, but rather\nexcitations of a quantum field."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 230280,
    "dDurationMs": 2940,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So you'd have an electron\nfield that permeates all"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 233220,
    "dDurationMs": 2880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of space, and this field can get excited,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 236100,
    "dDurationMs": 3180,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but only in identical, discrete units,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 239280,
    "dDurationMs": 3480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "each with the same mass, spin, and charge."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 242760,
    "dDurationMs": 2310,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And that's why every electron is the same."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 245070,
    "dDurationMs": 2789,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "They're all excitations of the same field."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 247859,
    "dDurationMs": 2581,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Now, you could have several excitations,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 250440,
    "dDurationMs": 1692,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that would be several electrons,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 252132,
    "dDurationMs": 2055,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and they can move around too."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 254187,
    "dDurationMs": 4143,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The only requirement is that\nthey can never overlap exactly."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 258330,
    "dDurationMs": 1950,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Of course, there is nothing special"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 260280,
    "dDurationMs": 1489,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "about this kind of excitation."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 261769,
    "dDurationMs": 3191,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "You could just as well\nhave a mirror opposite."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 264960,
    "dDurationMs": 2250,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "In fact, the equations that describe"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 267210,
    "dDurationMs": 3300,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "this field require such\nexcitations to exist."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 270510,
    "dDurationMs": 4470,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "They have the same mass and\nspin, but with opposite charge."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 274980,
    "dDurationMs": 4682,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This is the idea of an\nantielectron, or positron."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 279662,
    "dDurationMs": 1588,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It's exactly what"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 281250,
    "dDurationMs": 3270,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that minus sign in Dirac's\nequation was revealing."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 284520,
    "dDurationMs": 3450,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And just like an electron,\npositrons can move around too."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 287970,
    "dDurationMs": 3270,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Only positrons can overlap with electrons."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 291240,
    "dDurationMs": 2040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But watch what happens when they do."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 293280,
    "dDurationMs": 2310,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Now, I'm simplifying a little here,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 295590,
    "dDurationMs": 2640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but because they're each\nother's mirror images,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 298230,
    "dDurationMs": 2253,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the opposite charges\ncancel each other out,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 301362,
    "dDurationMs": 3067,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the excitations disappear,\nand the field returns back"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 304429,
    "dDurationMs": 1811,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to its ground state,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 306240,
    "dDurationMs": 3175,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but that would predict that\nthe particles just disappear."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 309415,
    "dDurationMs": 3373,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So how is that possible?\nWhere did the mass go?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 312788,
    "dDurationMs": 2399,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Well, the only way this could work"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 315187,
    "dDurationMs": 2063,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "is if that mass got converted"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 317250,
    "dDurationMs": 1860,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "into something else, energy,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 319110,
    "dDurationMs": 2461,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "according to E equals mc squared."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 321571,
    "dDurationMs": 1394,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The energy got transferred"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 322965,
    "dDurationMs": 4245,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "into a different quantum\nfield, the photon field,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 327210,
    "dDurationMs": 3240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and that is what we mean by annihilation."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 330450,
    "dDurationMs": 850,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Now, people realize"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 331300,
    "dDurationMs": 3470,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that most fundamental particles\ncould be described using"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 334770,
    "dDurationMs": 2460,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the same approach,\nwhere each could be seen"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 337230,
    "dDurationMs": 3335,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "as an excitation of their\nvery own quantum field."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 340565,
    "dDurationMs": 1944,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Now, this meant two things."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 342509,
    "dDurationMs": 2761,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The first is that most particles must"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 345270,
    "dDurationMs": 1530,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "have an antiparticle twin,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 346800,
    "dDurationMs": 3360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "because they're just mirror\nexcitations in the same field."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 350160,
    "dDurationMs": 2070,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "There are some exceptions though,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 352230,
    "dDurationMs": 2160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "like the photon and Higgs boson,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 354390,
    "dDurationMs": 2220,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "which are their own antiparticle."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 356610,
    "dDurationMs": 2676,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And the second and more\nimportant implication"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 359286,
    "dDurationMs": 3714,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "is that each antiparticle\nmust be exactly equal"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 363000,
    "dDurationMs": 3786,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to a normal particle, just\nwith the opposite charge."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 366786,
    "dDurationMs": 2574,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But then, around the mid 1960s,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 369360,
    "dDurationMs": 2460,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "people realized that there was a big issue"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 371820,
    "dDurationMs": 1380,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "with this explanation."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 373200,
    "dDurationMs": 1710,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And it all stemmed from how it fit"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 374910,
    "dDurationMs": 3333,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "in with the newly\naccepted Big Bang theory."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 379920,
    "dDurationMs": 2760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "In the very first moments\nafter the Big Bang,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 382680,
    "dDurationMs": 2700,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the universe was extremely hot and dense,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 385380,
    "dDurationMs": 3240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and photons had so much energy\nthat the reverse process"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 388620,
    "dDurationMs": 1410,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of annihilation happened."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 390030,
    "dDurationMs": 2010,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So two photons could come together"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 392040,
    "dDurationMs": 2640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and spontaneously convert\ntheir energy into the mass"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 394680,
    "dDurationMs": 3383,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and kinetic energy of a\nparticle-antiparticle pair."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 398063,
    "dDurationMs": 2047,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And so, the universe was filled"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 400110,
    "dDurationMs": 1770,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "with these pairs continuously popping"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 401880,
    "dDurationMs": 2111,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "into and out of existence."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 403991,
    "dDurationMs": 3949,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But as the universe continued\nto expand, it cooled,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 407940,
    "dDurationMs": 2370,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and those photons lost energy."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 410310,
    "dDurationMs": 2280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Until around three seconds\nafter the Big Bang,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 412590,
    "dDurationMs": 4563,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "they had lost so much energy\nthat pair production stopped."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 417153,
    "dDurationMs": 3927,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And this is what troubled\nphysicists in the 1960s,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 421080,
    "dDurationMs": 2790,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "because they believed that\nin those initial stages,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 423870,
    "dDurationMs": 3120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "an equal amount of matter\nand antimatter should"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 426990,
    "dDurationMs": 1470,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "have been created."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 428460,
    "dDurationMs": 2310,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But if an equal amount of matter"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 430770,
    "dDurationMs": 1556,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and antimatter were created,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 432326,
    "dDurationMs": 1984,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "then every particle should"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 434310,
    "dDurationMs": 3870,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "have found its antiparticle\ntwin, and annihilated."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 438180,
    "dDurationMs": 2430,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Meaning there should\nbe no stuff around us,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 440610,
    "dDurationMs": 5000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "no matter and no antimatter,\njust photons, only radiation."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 446130,
    "dDurationMs": 3693,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So this became known as the\nBig Bang radiation catastrophe."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 450962,
    "dDurationMs": 3031,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Because clearly, when we look around us,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 453993,
    "dDurationMs": 2487,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "we see a lot more than just energy."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 456480,
    "dDurationMs": 4020,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The universe is filled with\nmatter. But how can that be?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 460500,
    "dDurationMs": 2300,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Why is there now more\nmatter than antimatter"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 462800,
    "dDurationMs": 1420,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "in the universe?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 464220,
    "dDurationMs": 2460,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Where did that asymmetry come from?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 466680,
    "dDurationMs": 3194,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Well, that is one of the\nbiggest unsolved mysteries"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 469874,
    "dDurationMs": 2089,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "in all of physics."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 472860,
    "dDurationMs": 2850,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Initially, some people\ntried to brush this away,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 475710,
    "dDurationMs": 3772,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and they argued that perhaps\nthere is no asymmetry at all."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 479482,
    "dDurationMs": 1856,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- Maybe we happen to be in a pocket"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 481338,
    "dDurationMs": 2442,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that because of blind random chance,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 483780,
    "dDurationMs": 2610,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "some reasonable statistical fluctuations,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 486390,
    "dDurationMs": 1830,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "we're mostly surrounded by matter,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 488220,
    "dDurationMs": 1770,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and there'd be some region\nthat would, again, be like,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 489990,
    "dDurationMs": 2430,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "like a Marvel movie, like\nsome mirror universe,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 492420,
    "dDurationMs": 1620,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that we're most slightly, you know,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 494040,
    "dDurationMs": 2040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "imbalanced in the other direction."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 496080,
    "dDurationMs": 2101,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- [Casper] Paul Dirac seemed\nto have favored this approach."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 498181,
    "dDurationMs": 3149,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "He argued that there\nmight be entire antistars,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 501330,
    "dDurationMs": 3453,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and he ended his 1933\nNobel lecture by saying,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 504783,
    "dDurationMs": 3087,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "\"There may be half the stars of each kind."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 507870,
    "dDurationMs": 2460,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The two kinds of stars\nwould both show exactly"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 510330,
    "dDurationMs": 1759,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the same spectra, and\nthere would be no way"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 512089,
    "dDurationMs": 4631,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of distinguishing them by\npresent astronomical methods.\""
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 516720,
    "dDurationMs": 2760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Physicist Edward Harrison\ntook this one step further,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 519480,
    "dDurationMs": 3097,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "saying there should even\nbe entire antigalaxies."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 524100,
    "dDurationMs": 960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- And then people realized, well,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 525060,
    "dDurationMs": 833,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "if that's the case,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 525893,
    "dDurationMs": 1987,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "there'd be regions where these boundaries"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 527880,
    "dDurationMs": 1230,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "where the two regions would meet,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 529110,
    "dDurationMs": 1920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and that should be lighting up the sky."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 531030,
    "dDurationMs": 3390,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "There should be tons of\nmatter-antimatter annihilation."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 534420,
    "dDurationMs": 2464,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "There should be tons of\nvery high energy light."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 536884,
    "dDurationMs": 4016,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- So people surveyed the sky\nlooking for these hotspots,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 540900,
    "dDurationMs": 1530,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but they didn't find any."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 542430,
    "dDurationMs": 2580,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And so this possibility was ruled out."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 545010,
    "dDurationMs": 3570,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "There really is more matter\nthan antimatter in our universe."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 548580,
    "dDurationMs": 2160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "There really is an asymmetry."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 550740,
    "dDurationMs": 2583,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So the next obvious question is, well,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 553323,
    "dDurationMs": 2127,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "how large is that asymmetry?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 555450,
    "dDurationMs": 3090,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "If we go back to around 10\nseconds after the Big Bang,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 558540,
    "dDurationMs": 2073,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "we can figure it out."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 561780,
    "dDurationMs": 2520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "By this time, pair\nproduction had long stopped,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 564300,
    "dDurationMs": 1950,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "a full seven seconds ago."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 566250,
    "dDurationMs": 2011,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And by now, just about every antiparticle"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 568261,
    "dDurationMs": 2969,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "had annihilated with\nits particle counterpart"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 571230,
    "dDurationMs": 1860,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and turned into photons."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 573090,
    "dDurationMs": 1860,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Now the universe was filled"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 574950,
    "dDurationMs": 1800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "with just some leftover particles,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 576750,
    "dDurationMs": 2430,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "like electrons and protons whizzing around"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 579180,
    "dDurationMs": 3515,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "at incredible speeds, and\nthose remnant photons."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 582695,
    "dDurationMs": 2845,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But because these electrons\nand protons were traveling"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 585540,
    "dDurationMs": 3120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "so fast, they couldn't come\ntogether to form atoms."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 588660,
    "dDurationMs": 2730,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So you had this plasma\nof charged particles,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 591390,
    "dDurationMs": 2580,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and that meant that when\nphotons were going around,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 593970,
    "dDurationMs": 2340,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "they scattered off\nthose charged particles."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 596310,
    "dDurationMs": 1381,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So they couldn't travel very far"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 597691,
    "dDurationMs": 2275,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "without interacting with matter."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 599966,
    "dDurationMs": 4774,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "That all changed around 380,000\nyears after the Big Bang."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 604740,
    "dDurationMs": 2730,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "By now, the electrons and\nprotons had slowed down enough"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 607470,
    "dDurationMs": 1560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to form neutral atoms,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 609030,
    "dDurationMs": 2896,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and photons could only be\nabsorbed by electrons in atoms"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 611926,
    "dDurationMs": 2594,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "if they had exactly the\nright energy to move"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 614520,
    "dDurationMs": 2910,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the electron up an energy level."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 617430,
    "dDurationMs": 1170,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "In practice, this meant"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 618600,
    "dDurationMs": 2100,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that photons could now basically travel"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 620700,
    "dDurationMs": 1443,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "through space unimpeded."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 623010,
    "dDurationMs": 2580,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Those atoms then went\non to form all the stars"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 625590,
    "dDurationMs": 3600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and galaxies, and those\nphotons stuck around too."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 629190,
    "dDurationMs": 2296,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "They've gone on to make\nup the low-level radiation"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 631486,
    "dDurationMs": 3644,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that permeates the entire\nobservable universe,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 635130,
    "dDurationMs": 3303,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the Cosmic Microwave Background, or CMB."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 639390,
    "dDurationMs": 2646,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And when we estimate the\ntotal number of photons"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 642036,
    "dDurationMs": 4229,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "in that CMB, we find that\nthere are about 10 to the 89."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 646265,
    "dDurationMs": 1525,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And because almost all"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 647790,
    "dDurationMs": 1844,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of those photons were originally created"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 649634,
    "dDurationMs": 3136,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "during those very first\nseconds after the Big Bang,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 652770,
    "dDurationMs": 2730,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that original annihilation, we can infer"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 655500,
    "dDurationMs": 2640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that there must originally\nhave been around 10"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 658140,
    "dDurationMs": 3156,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to the 89 particles and antiparticles."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 661296,
    "dDurationMs": 1210,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Now, we can also estimate"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 662506,
    "dDurationMs": 2444,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "how many ordinary matter particles,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 664950,
    "dDurationMs": 1920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "like protons and neutrons,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 666870,
    "dDurationMs": 2580,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "there are in the\nobservable universe today,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 669450,
    "dDurationMs": 2880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the ones that survived that annihilation."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 672330,
    "dDurationMs": 3140,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And what we find is that\nthere are about 10 to the 80."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 675470,
    "dDurationMs": 1660,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So that means"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 677130,
    "dDurationMs": 2460,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that for every billion\nantimatter particles"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 679590,
    "dDurationMs": 1860,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and billion matter particles there were"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 681450,
    "dDurationMs": 2610,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "in the early universe,\nwhen they annihilated,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 684060,
    "dDurationMs": 1980,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "they did so almost perfectly."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 686040,
    "dDurationMs": 1052,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But there was one,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 687092,
    "dDurationMs": 4438,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "one out of a billion matter\nparticles that somehow survived."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 691530,
    "dDurationMs": 2817,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And everything we see around\nus today is a descendant"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 694347,
    "dDurationMs": 3903,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of those lucky one in a billion particles."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 698250,
    "dDurationMs": 2880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Every person, animal, jungle, and ocean,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 701130,
    "dDurationMs": 3210,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "every asteroid colliding\nor galaxy spiraling,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 704340,
    "dDurationMs": 3905,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "every single dot of light\nin the night sky is made up"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 708245,
    "dDurationMs": 4453,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of one of those lucky one\nin a billion particles."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 712698,
    "dDurationMs": 2742,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And that brings us to the craziest part."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 715440,
    "dDurationMs": 2670,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Because it tells us that\nthere must be a difference"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 718110,
    "dDurationMs": 2040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "between matter and antimatter."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 720150,
    "dDurationMs": 3090,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And how they evolve according\nto the laws of physics."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 723240,
    "dDurationMs": 1980,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But it's not just any difference."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 725220,
    "dDurationMs": 1230,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "No, it would make sense"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 726450,
    "dDurationMs": 1860,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "if they behaved completely different."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 728310,
    "dDurationMs": 1800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "I mean, you would just have different laws"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 730110,
    "dDurationMs": 2700,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of physics governing\neach type of particle."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 732810,
    "dDurationMs": 2070,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Or it would make sense\nif they were governed"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 734880,
    "dDurationMs": 1800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "by the exact same laws."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 736680,
    "dDurationMs": 2430,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But in that case, there\nwould be no difference."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 739110,
    "dDurationMs": 2310,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It would be completely symmetric."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 741420,
    "dDurationMs": 2400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "What's really weird here is that the laws"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 743820,
    "dDurationMs": 4320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "are almost exactly the same,\nbut with a tiny difference."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 748140,
    "dDurationMs": 2602,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And that doesn't make any sense."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 750742,
    "dDurationMs": 1778,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "For the past 70 years,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 752520,
    "dDurationMs": 1920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "physicists have tried to explain"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 754440,
    "dDurationMs": 1748,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "where this asymmetry comes from."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 756188,
    "dDurationMs": 3160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But so far, all attempts have failed."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 759348,
    "dDurationMs": 2465,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And part of the reason\nthis has been so difficult"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 761813,
    "dDurationMs": 3670,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "is because our laws of\nphysics are full of symmetry."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 768030,
    "dDurationMs": 1530,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "In the mid 1950s,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 769560,
    "dDurationMs": 1590,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "there were three symmetries all"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 771150,
    "dDurationMs": 2100,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "particles were believed to obey."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 773250,
    "dDurationMs": 3210,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Charge, parity, and\ntime reversal symmetry."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 776460,
    "dDurationMs": 2340,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Charge symmetry is super simple."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 778800,
    "dDurationMs": 2820,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It just means that if you\nswap all positive charges"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 781620,
    "dDurationMs": 1946,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "with negative ones, and vice versa,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 783566,
    "dDurationMs": 2794,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "then the interactions don't change."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 786360,
    "dDurationMs": 2906,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "In other words, there is\nnothing special about a positive"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 789266,
    "dDurationMs": 1654,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "or negative charge."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 790920,
    "dDurationMs": 4100,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Just that one is exactly equal\nand opposite to the other."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 795020,
    "dDurationMs": 3340,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "To understand parity symmetry,\nconsider this mirror,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 798360,
    "dDurationMs": 2370,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "which creates a sort of parallel universe"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 800730,
    "dDurationMs": 2700,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "where everything is the\nsame, but reflected."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 803430,
    "dDurationMs": 3450,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So my left hand becomes my\nright hand and vice versa."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 806880,
    "dDurationMs": 3120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Now take this molecule\nhere, which is L-alanine,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 810000,
    "dDurationMs": 3150,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "an important amino acid\nwe need to make proteins."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 813150,
    "dDurationMs": 2970,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Now that L is in its name\nbecause the amine group,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 816120,
    "dDurationMs": 2790,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "this NH2 part over here, is on the left."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 818910,
    "dDurationMs": 3480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But in the mirror, you see its\nsister molecule, D-alanine,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 822390,
    "dDurationMs": 2730,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that NH2 part is now on the right."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 825120,
    "dDurationMs": 2070,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And if you try to make alanine in a lab,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 827190,
    "dDurationMs": 4800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "you'll find that you'll get 50%\nL-alanine and 50% D-alanine."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 831990,
    "dDurationMs": 2610,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "In other words, there is\nno experiment you could do"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 834600,
    "dDurationMs": 2430,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that determines whether\nyou're in our universe"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 837030,
    "dDurationMs": 1981,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "or in the mirror universe."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 839011,
    "dDurationMs": 2429,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And the same is true for many left"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 841440,
    "dDurationMs": 1290,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and right handed molecules."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 842730,
    "dDurationMs": 2430,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "If you just try to make\nthem normally in a lab,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 845160,
    "dDurationMs": 2130,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "you'll get 50% of each."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 847290,
    "dDurationMs": 3644,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So our universe doesn't favor\nleft or right handedness."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 850934,
    "dDurationMs": 3166,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Lastly, time reversal\nsymmetry means that the laws"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 854100,
    "dDurationMs": 833,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of physics work"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 854933,
    "dDurationMs": 3068,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the same whether time is\nrunning forwards or backwards."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 858001,
    "dDurationMs": 1718,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Now, out of all of these,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 859719,
    "dDurationMs": 2961,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "time reversal symmetry might feel strange."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 862680,
    "dDurationMs": 1590,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Because there are many things"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 864270,
    "dDurationMs": 2880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that clearly don't work backwards in time."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 867150,
    "dDurationMs": 3000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "You can't uncook an egg,\nunshatter a wine glass,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 870150,
    "dDurationMs": 2940,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "or turn a plant back into a seed."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 873090,
    "dDurationMs": 2409,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But all of these follow\nfrom the second law"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 875499,
    "dDurationMs": 1960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of thermodynamics, which describes"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 877459,
    "dDurationMs": 2201,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "how many interacting particles evolve"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 879660,
    "dDurationMs": 2970,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "from less likely states,\ntypically more ordered,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 882630,
    "dDurationMs": 2625,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to more likely states, typically a mess."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 885255,
    "dDurationMs": 2115,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But this is a statistical law,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 887370,
    "dDurationMs": 2610,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "it's not a fundamental law of physics."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 889980,
    "dDurationMs": 3240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "If you zoom in to the level\nof individual particles,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 893220,
    "dDurationMs": 2940,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "then every interaction\nis perfectly reversible."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 896160,
    "dDurationMs": 2610,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "You can tell whether these\ncollisions happen forwards"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 898770,
    "dDurationMs": 1770,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "or backwards in time."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 900540,
    "dDurationMs": 2790,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Now the combination of all\nof these symmetries combined"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 903330,
    "dDurationMs": 1982,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "is called CPT symmetry."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 905312,
    "dDurationMs": 4618,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And CPT symmetry, it turns\nout, is kind of a big deal."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 909930,
    "dDurationMs": 2040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "What happens if CPT gets broken?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 911970,
    "dDurationMs": 930,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- Well literally cats"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 912900,
    "dDurationMs": 1890,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and dogs start living\ntogether, time flows backwards."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 914790,
    "dDurationMs": 2010,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "All kinds of things start breaking"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 916800,
    "dDurationMs": 1320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "in our description of nature."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 918120,
    "dDurationMs": 3845,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Now one of the reasons why\nCPT and the standard model go"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 921965,
    "dDurationMs": 3355,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "so well together is\nbecause it really is built"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 925320,
    "dDurationMs": 2670,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "into the very structure\nof special relativity."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 927990,
    "dDurationMs": 1489,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- The special relativity is built"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 929479,
    "dDurationMs": 1987,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "on one core principle."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 931466,
    "dDurationMs": 2389,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Which is that the laws\nof physics are the same"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 933855,
    "dDurationMs": 2415,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "for all inertial observers."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 936270,
    "dDurationMs": 2040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And this includes any measurement"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 938310,
    "dDurationMs": 1623,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "they make of the speed of light."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 941130,
    "dDurationMs": 2279,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "In the 1950s, Julian Schwinger,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 943409,
    "dDurationMs": 3061,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Gerhart Lüders, and Wolfgang Pauli proved"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 946470,
    "dDurationMs": 2490,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that if our universe obeys this principle,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 948960,
    "dDurationMs": 1716,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "which we strongly believe it does,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 950676,
    "dDurationMs": 2574,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "then it must be CPT symmetric."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 953250,
    "dDurationMs": 1950,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But the reverse is also true."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 955200,
    "dDurationMs": 2280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "If you break CPT symmetry,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 957480,
    "dDurationMs": 2403,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "then this core principle also breaks."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 959883,
    "dDurationMs": 2217,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And that's where things get tricky."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 962100,
    "dDurationMs": 2380,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Because after Dirac\nunited special relativity"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 964480,
    "dDurationMs": 3740,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "with quantum mechanics, all\nfollowing quantum theories also"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 968220,
    "dDurationMs": 1800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "incorporated special relativity."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 970020,
    "dDurationMs": 2490,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And so our best theories of reality,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 972510,
    "dDurationMs": 2400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "quantum field theory\nand the standard model,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 974910,
    "dDurationMs": 2885,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "are built on that exact same principle."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 977795,
    "dDurationMs": 2155,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So now we have a paradox."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 979950,
    "dDurationMs": 3000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Because on the one hand we\nneed asymmetry to explain"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 982950,
    "dDurationMs": 1560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "why we're here."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 984510,
    "dDurationMs": 2579,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But on the other hand,\nif CPT symmetry breaks,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 987089,
    "dDurationMs": 3181,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "it tears down our best theories with it."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 990270,
    "dDurationMs": 2400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So physicists started off on a hunt"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 992670,
    "dDurationMs": 2340,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "for a special kind of asymmetry."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 995010,
    "dDurationMs": 1819,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "An asymmetry that could explain that one"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 996829,
    "dDurationMs": 1691,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "in a billion discrepancy,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 998520,
    "dDurationMs": 3543,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "while also maintaining\nthe larger CPT symmetry."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1002930,
    "dDurationMs": 2610,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The first clue that such\nasymmetries might exist came"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1005540,
    "dDurationMs": 1761,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "in the mid 1950s."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1007301,
    "dDurationMs": 2109,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Up until then, every interaction"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1009410,
    "dDurationMs": 2610,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that had been studied conserved\nthe individual symmetries"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1012020,
    "dDurationMs": 2010,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of C, P and T."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1014030,
    "dDurationMs": 2610,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And so conserved CPT as a whole."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1016640,
    "dDurationMs": 3660,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But in 1956, theoretical\nphysicists Tsung-Dao Lee"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1020300,
    "dDurationMs": 3180,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and Chen-Ning Yang realized\nthat no one had checked"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1023480,
    "dDurationMs": 3540,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "whether parity is conserved\nin the weak nuclear force."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1027020,
    "dDurationMs": 2928,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So they set out to test whether\nthe universe favored left"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1029948,
    "dDurationMs": 2052,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "or right handedness."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1032000,
    "dDurationMs": 833,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And to do it,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1032833,
    "dDurationMs": 2857,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "they enlisted the help of\none of Lee's colleagues,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1035690,
    "dDurationMs": 4080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "one of the world's best\nexperimentalists, Chien-Shiung Wu,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1039770,
    "dDurationMs": 2250,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "also known as Madame Wu."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1042020,
    "dDurationMs": 2580,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- Once the idea of the\nexperiment was pitched"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1044600,
    "dDurationMs": 1680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to her, then she just went all in."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1046280,
    "dDurationMs": 2850,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "She canceled trips, she worked\nstraight over holiday breaks."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1049130,
    "dDurationMs": 3090,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It was really an all\nhands on deck operation"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1052220,
    "dDurationMs": 2400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "over a very frenzied few months."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1054620,
    "dDurationMs": 2010,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- When Pauli learned of the experiment,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1056630,
    "dDurationMs": 2280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "he said, \"I do not believe that the Lord"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1058910,
    "dDurationMs": 1320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "is a weak left-hander,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1060230,
    "dDurationMs": 2138,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and I am ready to bet a very high sum"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1062368,
    "dDurationMs": 3619,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that the experiments will\ngive symmetric results.\""
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1067220,
    "dDurationMs": 3450,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Now all that was left to\ndo was run the experiment."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1070670,
    "dDurationMs": 2580,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It worked something like this."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1073250,
    "dDurationMs": 2070,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "She started with cobalt 60,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1075320,
    "dDurationMs": 2250,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "an isotope of cobalt where the nucleus"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1077570,
    "dDurationMs": 3240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "has an intrinsic angular\nmomentum, or spin."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1080810,
    "dDurationMs": 2490,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "When she applied a strong magnetic field,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1083300,
    "dDurationMs": 3330,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "she forced all the spins to\npoint in the same direction."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1086630,
    "dDurationMs": 2760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But cobalt 60 is also radioactive."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1089390,
    "dDurationMs": 1560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So every once in a while,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1090950,
    "dDurationMs": 2850,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "a neutron inside one of its nuclei decays"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1093800,
    "dDurationMs": 3690,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "into a proton, releasing an\nelectron and antineutrino,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1097490,
    "dDurationMs": 3090,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and leaving a nickel 60 atom behind."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1100580,
    "dDurationMs": 3450,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Now the electrons emitted\ncould travel in two directions."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1104030,
    "dDurationMs": 2490,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "They could either go in the same direction"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1106520,
    "dDurationMs": 4230,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "as the nuclear spin, or they\ncould go in the opposite way."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1110750,
    "dDurationMs": 2573,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But if spin is clockwise in our universe,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1113323,
    "dDurationMs": 3637,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "then it is also clockwise\nwhen reflected in the mirror."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1116960,
    "dDurationMs": 2430,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Which means it points\nin the same direction"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1119390,
    "dDurationMs": 1560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "in both universes."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1120950,
    "dDurationMs": 2670,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So the only way the\nexperiment could be the same"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1123620,
    "dDurationMs": 2430,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "in our universe and the mirror universe,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1126050,
    "dDurationMs": 2910,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "is if the electrons were\nemitted in equal amounts"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1128960,
    "dDurationMs": 1140,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "in each direction."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1130100,
    "dDurationMs": 3180,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It should be 50% on each side."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1133280,
    "dDurationMs": 2990,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But what Wu actually\nfound was that around 60%"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1136270,
    "dDurationMs": 2684,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of the electrons moved\nin the opposite direction"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1138954,
    "dDurationMs": 1435,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to the nuclear spin."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1140389,
    "dDurationMs": 3691,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Which would mean that 60%\nmoved in the same direction"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1144080,
    "dDurationMs": 2542,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "as the nuclear spin in\nthe mirror universe."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1146622,
    "dDurationMs": 3128,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But that meant that there is\nan experiment you could do"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1149750,
    "dDurationMs": 1687,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to tell whether you are in our universe"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1151437,
    "dDurationMs": 1853,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "or the mirror universe."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1153290,
    "dDurationMs": 2994,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So it proved that parity is not conserved."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1156284,
    "dDurationMs": 2943,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This shocked the physics community."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1159227,
    "dDurationMs": 1863,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Pauli, upon being informed"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1161090,
    "dDurationMs": 3188,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of the results, exclaimed,\n\"That's total nonsense!\""
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1164278,
    "dDurationMs": 2932,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- Very smart people, Nobel Laureates said,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1167210,
    "dDurationMs": 1453,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that can't be right."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1168663,
    "dDurationMs": 2490,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Do it again. I don't believe it."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1171153,
    "dDurationMs": 3317,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "You know, and in a sense you can see"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1174470,
    "dDurationMs": 833,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "where they're coming from."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1175303,
    "dDurationMs": 2740,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "There have been no hint\nas yet that kind of"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1178043,
    "dDurationMs": 1647,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the universe would care"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1179690,
    "dDurationMs": 1890,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "whether I'm looking at myself, you know,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1181580,
    "dDurationMs": 1590,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "in a mirror or not."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1183170,
    "dDurationMs": 1860,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- So others repeated the experiment"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1185030,
    "dDurationMs": 4050,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and by 1957 there was no\nfurther room for doubt."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1189080,
    "dDurationMs": 2643,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "God really was a weak left-hander."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1193130,
    "dDurationMs": 2460,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "That same year, Lee and\nYang won the Nobel Prize"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1195590,
    "dDurationMs": 2625,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "in Physics for the discovery\nof parity violation."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1198215,
    "dDurationMs": 2535,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But Wu's name was left off."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1200750,
    "dDurationMs": 2670,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Lee and Young acknowledged\nher during their speech"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1203420,
    "dDurationMs": 2850,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and tried to get her nominated\nfor a prize another year."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1206270,
    "dDurationMs": 2040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But the Nobel committee never honored her."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1208310,
    "dDurationMs": 3330,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "In a way, she was robbed\nof the Nobel Prize."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1211640,
    "dDurationMs": 2190,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "1988 winner Jack Steinberger called"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1213830,
    "dDurationMs": 3193,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "this the biggest mistake in\nthe Nobel committee's history."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1217023,
    "dDurationMs": 2645,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But her work had done something important."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1219668,
    "dDurationMs": 2622,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It had cast doubt on the long-held belief"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1222290,
    "dDurationMs": 1500,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that charge, parity,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1223790,
    "dDurationMs": 2670,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and time reversal were\nfundamental symmetries"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1226460,
    "dDurationMs": 1830,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of our universe."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1228290,
    "dDurationMs": 2430,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This made many physicists uncomfortable."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1230720,
    "dDurationMs": 2430,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So they came up with a workaround."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1233150,
    "dDurationMs": 3240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Maybe it's okay if parity\nsymmetry was broken."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1236390,
    "dDurationMs": 2520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Because that's not a\nfundamental symmetry of nature."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1238910,
    "dDurationMs": 3675,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It's just part of a larger\nsymmetry, charge parity."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1242585,
    "dDurationMs": 2835,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The idea was that if\nyou reflected everything"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1245420,
    "dDurationMs": 2520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "in a mirror and swapped all the particles"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1247940,
    "dDurationMs": 1770,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "for their antiparticles, then"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1249710,
    "dDurationMs": 2950,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the symmetry would be restored\nand all would be good again."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1254120,
    "dDurationMs": 1740,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But then, seven years later,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1255860,
    "dDurationMs": 3270,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "two physicists found that\nsome particles also violated"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1259130,
    "dDurationMs": 2181,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the combined charge parity symmetry."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1261311,
    "dDurationMs": 3249,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Now physicists were\ngetting really nervous."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1264560,
    "dDurationMs": 2760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Two symmetries that they\nbelieved were fundamental parts"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1267320,
    "dDurationMs": 1710,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of our universe were broken."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1269030,
    "dDurationMs": 2882,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So the next big question\non everyone's mind was,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1271912,
    "dDurationMs": 4227,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "is CPT symmetry also going\nto fail and take down"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1276139,
    "dDurationMs": 2371,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the standard model with it?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1278510,
    "dDurationMs": 4380,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Then, in 1973, something\nseemingly miraculous happened."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1282890,
    "dDurationMs": 3420,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Makoto Kobayashi and\nToshihide Maskawa found a way"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1286310,
    "dDurationMs": 3664,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to explain all the\nobserved P and CP violation"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1289974,
    "dDurationMs": 2726,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "while maintaining CPT symmetry."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1292700,
    "dDurationMs": 3690,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And it all fit directly\nwithin the standard model."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1296390,
    "dDurationMs": 2060,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The only issue is that when it comes"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1298450,
    "dDurationMs": 2410,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to the matter-antimatter asymmetry,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1300860,
    "dDurationMs": 4110,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "it can only account for an\nasymmetry of 10 to the minus 18."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1304970,
    "dDurationMs": 2730,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Which is a billion times less than we need"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1307700,
    "dDurationMs": 3789,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to explain the observed\nmatter-antimatter asymmetry."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1311489,
    "dDurationMs": 1693,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- So the ingredients are there,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1313182,
    "dDurationMs": 1778,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "which is cool because we didn't think even"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1314960,
    "dDurationMs": 833,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the ingredients were there."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1315793,
    "dDurationMs": 1357,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- Right.\n- But they're not there"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1317150,
    "dDurationMs": 1710,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "in a large enough strength."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1318860,
    "dDurationMs": 3600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "You don't have a strong\nenough rate of CP violation"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1322460,
    "dDurationMs": 2790,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "if you just stick with\nstrictly the standard model."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1325250,
    "dDurationMs": 2760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- And so are people now\ngetting nervous about CPT?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1328010,
    "dDurationMs": 1920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- Not nervous, I'd say excited."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1329930,
    "dDurationMs": 1620,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- And that's because this means there"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1331550,
    "dDurationMs": 3120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "is likely new physics\nbeyond the standard model."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1334670,
    "dDurationMs": 1831,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But to find out what that might be,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1336501,
    "dDurationMs": 2969,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "we must study antimatter up close,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1339470,
    "dDurationMs": 1710,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to see if there are any ways"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1341180,
    "dDurationMs": 2460,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "in which it might be\ndifferent from normal matter."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1343640,
    "dDurationMs": 2520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Ways that could explain that asymmetry."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1346160,
    "dDurationMs": 4468,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So, you know where we're\ngoing. Oh, look, there it is."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1350628,
    "dDurationMs": 1702,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "CERN, baby.\n- Woo-hoo!"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1352330,
    "dDurationMs": 3160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- CERN is best known for\nthe Large Hadron Collider,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1355490,
    "dDurationMs": 3390,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "a 27 kilometer underground\nring where protons"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1358880,
    "dDurationMs": 5000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "are accelerated up to\n99.999999% the speed of light."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1364910,
    "dDurationMs": 2010,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Beams traveling in opposite directions"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1366920,
    "dDurationMs": 3610,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "are smashed together, releasing\nhuge amounts of energy."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1370530,
    "dDurationMs": 3140,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It's the closest we get to\nthe high energy conditions"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1373670,
    "dDurationMs": 1770,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of the early universe."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1375440,
    "dDurationMs": 2310,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But at the southern edge of the LHC,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1377750,
    "dDurationMs": 2700,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "there is a smaller\nproton accelerator called"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1380450,
    "dDurationMs": 1657,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the proton synchrotron."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1382107,
    "dDurationMs": 4743,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Protons in this ring are\nonly accelerated to 99.93%"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1386850,
    "dDurationMs": 1610,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the speed of light."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1388460,
    "dDurationMs": 2790,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And some of that proton\nbeam is fed out of the ring"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1391250,
    "dDurationMs": 2040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and ends up here."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1393290,
    "dDurationMs": 2760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This is CERN's antimatter factory."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1396050,
    "dDurationMs": 3204,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And in here, you make\nantiprotons. How many?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1399254,
    "dDurationMs": 4086,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- Usually it's around 40\nmillion every couple of minutes."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1403340,
    "dDurationMs": 3720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "We are now going to enter\nthe facility by actually"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1407060,
    "dDurationMs": 900,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "a technical building,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1407960,
    "dDurationMs": 2460,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "which is not very interesting to watch."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1410420,
    "dDurationMs": 2160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- [Casper] I find this\nall interesting to watch."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1412580,
    "dDurationMs": 1350,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "To make sure we're safe,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1413930,
    "dDurationMs": 2220,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "we always had to carry\naround these devices."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1416150,
    "dDurationMs": 3298,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So you've got two, what are they called?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1419448,
    "dDurationMs": 1442,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- Dosimeters.\n- Dosimeters?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1420890,
    "dDurationMs": 1980,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- Yes.\n- Yeah, just to be safe."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1422870,
    "dDurationMs": 2370,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- These are standard devices to measure"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1425240,
    "dDurationMs": 3420,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the amount of dose of\nradiation that you get."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1428660,
    "dDurationMs": 3480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This is a supervised\nradiation environment,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1432140,
    "dDurationMs": 2942,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "which means it's an environment\nin which we keep an eye"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1435082,
    "dDurationMs": 3328,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "on to the amount of radiation\nwe get as radiation workers."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1438410,
    "dDurationMs": 833,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- Where are we going now?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1439243,
    "dDurationMs": 5000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- So now we are going to\nenter into the main building."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1444260,
    "dDurationMs": 2133,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- [Casper] There's\nantimatter behind this door?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1446393,
    "dDurationMs": 2217,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- Yes, yes, under our feet."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1448610,
    "dDurationMs": 2021,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- Oh wow.\n- Yeah, you'll see,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1450631,
    "dDurationMs": 833,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "you'll see."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1452780,
    "dDurationMs": 2221,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Please guys, welcome."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1455001,
    "dDurationMs": 2036,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- This is huge.\n- This is a huge place."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1457037,
    "dDurationMs": 2496,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "(dramatic music)"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1459533,
    "dDurationMs": 2460,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- This is so much bigger\nthan I was thinking."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1463160,
    "dDurationMs": 963,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This is crazy."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1466130,
    "dDurationMs": 1050,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Well, I feel like I'm a kid"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1467180,
    "dDurationMs": 2400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "in a candy store looking at this."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1469580,
    "dDurationMs": 1680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- This place is pretty, is pretty fun,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1471260,
    "dDurationMs": 833,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the first time you see it."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1472093,
    "dDurationMs": 2055,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- Yeah, it's so impressive."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1474148,
    "dDurationMs": 2242,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- Here you see pretty much the scheme"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1476390,
    "dDurationMs": 1950,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of how this facility is working."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1478340,
    "dDurationMs": 1277,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "You get protons coming from one"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1479617,
    "dDurationMs": 3523,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of the CERN accelerators, the PS,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1483140,
    "dDurationMs": 2490,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "which smash onto a target..."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1485630,
    "dDurationMs": 1740,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- The protons are accelerated up"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1487370,
    "dDurationMs": 4590,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to around 99.93% the speed\nof light and have energies up"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1491960,
    "dDurationMs": 3060,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to 26 gigaelectronvolts."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1495020,
    "dDurationMs": 2160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "They're aimed at a\nremarkably small target,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1497180,
    "dDurationMs": 2820,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "an iridium rod, 3 millimeters in diameter"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1500000,
    "dDurationMs": 2460,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and 55 millimeters across,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1502460,
    "dDurationMs": 2760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "which itself is embedded\nin a graphite and then"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1505220,
    "dDurationMs": 2085,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "in a titanium alloy structure."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1507305,
    "dDurationMs": 1515,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Iridium was chosen"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1508820,
    "dDurationMs": 2940,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "because it's the second\ndensest element on Earth."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1511760,
    "dDurationMs": 3060,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And that means that there\nare a lot of nuclei packed"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1514820,
    "dDurationMs": 1290,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "in a small space,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1516110,
    "dDurationMs": 1260,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "which increases the odds"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1517370,
    "dDurationMs": 1923,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that the protons will hit something."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1519293,
    "dDurationMs": 3957,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But when one of these protons\nhits an iridium nucleus,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1523250,
    "dDurationMs": 3267,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "it doesn't bounce off like\nyou'd expect in most collisions."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1526517,
    "dDurationMs": 3153,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It is going so fast and has so much energy"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1529670,
    "dDurationMs": 2340,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that it penetrates the nucleus,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1532010,
    "dDurationMs": 1710,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "where it collides directly"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1533720,
    "dDurationMs": 2640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "with one of the neutrons or protons."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1536360,
    "dDurationMs": 1890,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And to understand what happens next,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1538250,
    "dDurationMs": 3627,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "we need to look at what's\ngoing on inside the proton."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1541877,
    "dDurationMs": 3513,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Because a proton is not\na fundamental particle."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1545390,
    "dDurationMs": 1020,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Instead, it is made up"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1546410,
    "dDurationMs": 3090,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of three fundamental\nparticles known as quarks,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1549500,
    "dDurationMs": 3090,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "specifically two up and one down quark."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1552590,
    "dDurationMs": 2880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Those quarks whiz around\nclose to the speed of light."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1555470,
    "dDurationMs": 2250,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So to keep all those quarks contained,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1557720,
    "dDurationMs": 2443,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "traveling at such incredible\nspeeds and in such"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1560163,
    "dDurationMs": 4487,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "a small space requires\na very strong force."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1564650,
    "dDurationMs": 2940,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Which is why it's called the strong force."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1567590,
    "dDurationMs": 3600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And it's mediated by\nparticles known as gluons."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1571190,
    "dDurationMs": 4020,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "You can think of this force\nas acting like a rubber band."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1575210,
    "dDurationMs": 2970,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But you can bring this\npast its breaking point."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1578180,
    "dDurationMs": 1890,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "If you keep putting in energy,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1580070,
    "dDurationMs": 2130,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "then you can put in so much energy"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1582200,
    "dDurationMs": 3540,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that another quark-antiquark\npair will be created."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1585740,
    "dDurationMs": 1260,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This bond breaking"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1587000,
    "dDurationMs": 3090,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "into pair creation can\nhappen several times in a row"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1590090,
    "dDurationMs": 1980,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and results in this sort of shower"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1592070,
    "dDurationMs": 1991,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of quark-antiquark pairs."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1594061,
    "dDurationMs": 3049,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And a similar thing happens\nwhen a proton collides"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1597110,
    "dDurationMs": 3540,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "with a neutron or proton\ninside an iridium nucleus."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1600650,
    "dDurationMs": 3270,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Now, most of those pairs\nstay just like that, pairs,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1603920,
    "dDurationMs": 1620,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and they travel off."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1605540,
    "dDurationMs": 1080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But occasionally,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1606620,
    "dDurationMs": 3090,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "you will get two antiup\nand one antidown quark"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1609710,
    "dDurationMs": 1590,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to come close enough."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1611300,
    "dDurationMs": 4230,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And they form a new particle\nmade of three antiquarks."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1615530,
    "dDurationMs": 2280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "They form an antiproton."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1617810,
    "dDurationMs": 2943,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And their counterparts will\ngo on to form a proton."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1621830,
    "dDurationMs": 1290,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Now, all of this,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1623120,
    "dDurationMs": 3780,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "this entire process from\ninitial collision to the shower"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1626900,
    "dDurationMs": 2481,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of particles and the\nformation of the antiproton,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1629381,
    "dDurationMs": 4382,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "happened in the span of 10\nto the minus 23 seconds."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1633763,
    "dDurationMs": 3907,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "That is a hundred billionth\ntrillionth of a second."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1637670,
    "dDurationMs": 2145,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It is absolutely insane."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1639815,
    "dDurationMs": 2205,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And every time you hit the target,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1642020,
    "dDurationMs": 1946,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "you get trillions of these collisions."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1643966,
    "dDurationMs": 3724,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And out the other side\ncomes a chaotic spray"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1647690,
    "dDurationMs": 3930,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of protons, antiprotons and\na bunch of other particles,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1651620,
    "dDurationMs": 3990,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "all traveling at around\n96% the speed of light."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1655610,
    "dDurationMs": 2160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Magnets then filter out the antiprotons"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1657770,
    "dDurationMs": 1900,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "from the other particles and they're sent"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1659670,
    "dDurationMs": 1940,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "on to the next stage."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1661610,
    "dDurationMs": 2010,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- And then we collect these antiprotons,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1663620,
    "dDurationMs": 1710,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "bring them into the ring,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1665330,
    "dDurationMs": 1380,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the antiproton decelerator ring,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1666710,
    "dDurationMs": 2310,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "which is the one we are staring on top of."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1669020,
    "dDurationMs": 2820,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And then they circulate\nin there for a while,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1671840,
    "dDurationMs": 1650,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "while they get cooled down."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1673490,
    "dDurationMs": 1331,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So the idea here is really"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1674821,
    "dDurationMs": 2689,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that we get these antiprotons\nevery two minutes,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1677510,
    "dDurationMs": 833,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "more or less."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1678343,
    "dDurationMs": 1807,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It's about 30 million of them."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1680150,
    "dDurationMs": 2490,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- How expensive is it, antimatter?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1682640,
    "dDurationMs": 2010,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- Look guys, what is value?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1684650,
    "dDurationMs": 1890,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It's a bit difficult\nto evaluate it, right?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1686540,
    "dDurationMs": 2970,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "For sure it's probably the\nmost expensive state of matter"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1689510,
    "dDurationMs": 1560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "we can build on Earth today."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1691070,
    "dDurationMs": 2040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- How about I name some\nnumbers and you tell me"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1693110,
    "dDurationMs": 2430,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "if it's cheap or too expensive?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1695540,
    "dDurationMs": 997,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- Shoot."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1696537,
    "dDurationMs": 2393,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- $1 billion per gram."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1698930,
    "dDurationMs": 843,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- No way."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1699773,
    "dDurationMs": 1516,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- It's too cheap?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1701289,
    "dDurationMs": 1919,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- Orders of magnitude too cheap."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1703208,
    "dDurationMs": 2036,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Like many orders of magnitude too cheap."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1705244,
    "dDurationMs": 1853,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- Yeah, that's what I was thinking."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1707097,
    "dDurationMs": 2063,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "$100 billion per gram."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1709160,
    "dDurationMs": 2010,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- No way, go up."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1711170,
    "dDurationMs": 4410,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "I think probably you\nmiss other three zeros."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1715580,
    "dDurationMs": 1110,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- Three zeros?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1716690,
    "dDurationMs": 1620,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- I think so, per gram, yes."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1718310,
    "dDurationMs": 1300,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "At least.\n- That's crazy."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1720560,
    "dDurationMs": 1710,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "If you're wondering what\nyou would do with all"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1722270,
    "dDurationMs": 1530,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that money, you should check"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1723800,
    "dDurationMs": 2400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "out today's video sponsor, SoFi."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1726200,
    "dDurationMs": 2970,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "SoFi is an all-in-one finance\napp that lets you bank,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1729170,
    "dDurationMs": 1350,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "borrow and invest."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1730520,
    "dDurationMs": 2700,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And with their premium\nmembership, SoFi Plus,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1733220,
    "dDurationMs": 2201,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "you get benefits such\nas investment matches,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1735421,
    "dDurationMs": 2329,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "unlimited access to financial planners"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1737750,
    "dDurationMs": 3210,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and a competitive APY on\nsavings to earn interest"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1740960,
    "dDurationMs": 930,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "on your money."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1741890,
    "dDurationMs": 2580,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "All so you can let your\nmoney work for you."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1744470,
    "dDurationMs": 1830,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "By adding up all of these benefits,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1746300,
    "dDurationMs": 3450,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "you could unlock $1,000\nor more in annual value"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1749750,
    "dDurationMs": 1740,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "with qualifying activities."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1751490,
    "dDurationMs": 2010,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Of course, it depends\non how you use the app,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1753500,
    "dDurationMs": 2037,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "so check if it's right for you."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1755537,
    "dDurationMs": 2973,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And you can get started by\nsubscribing to SoFi Plus,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1758510,
    "dDurationMs": 2112,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "for just $10 per month."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1760622,
    "dDurationMs": 2568,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Right now, they're also\nrunning a promotion"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1763190,
    "dDurationMs": 1470,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "for US residents."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1764660,
    "dDurationMs": 3605,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So if you join SoFi Plus\nbetween now and April 15th,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1768265,
    "dDurationMs": 2515,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "you'll automatically be\nentered into their giveaway"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1770780,
    "dDurationMs": 833,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "for a chance"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1771613,
    "dDurationMs": 3347,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to win $75,000 as well\nas other cash prizes"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1774960,
    "dDurationMs": 1910,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and free memberships."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1776870,
    "dDurationMs": 1680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So to check out SoFi Plus,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1778550,
    "dDurationMs": 3450,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "head to sofi.com/veritasium\nor click the link"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1782000,
    "dDurationMs": 990,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "in the description."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1782990,
    "dDurationMs": 2129,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "I'd like to thank SoFi\nfor sponsoring this video."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1785119,
    "dDurationMs": 2704,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And now back to antimatter."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1793130,
    "dDurationMs": 2779,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- There's antiprotons\ngoing beneath our feet."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1795909,
    "dDurationMs": 967,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- Yes."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1796876,
    "dDurationMs": 1594,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "They are under our feet\nat this time. Yes, indeed."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1798470,
    "dDurationMs": 1230,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- [Casper] And that's not dangerous?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1799700,
    "dDurationMs": 833,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- No, no, it's not dangerous."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1800533,
    "dDurationMs": 2347,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "There is no risk whatsoever."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1802880,
    "dDurationMs": 1410,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- Strong electric fields"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1804290,
    "dDurationMs": 3327,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "in the decelerator slow down\nthe antiprotons from 96%"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1807617,
    "dDurationMs": 3303,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to 10% the speed of light."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1810920,
    "dDurationMs": 4080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But that's still about 100\nmillion kilometers per hour."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1815000,
    "dDurationMs": 1560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "To do experiments with them,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1816560,
    "dDurationMs": 1962,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "they need to be slowed down more."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1818522,
    "dDurationMs": 4098,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Initially, this was done\nin a kind of crazy way."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1822620,
    "dDurationMs": 3720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The antiproton beam was\nfired at a thin plastic foil,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1826340,
    "dDurationMs": 4080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "which annihilated 99.9%\nof all the antiprotons."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1830420,
    "dDurationMs": 3390,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But around 0.1% of those\nantiprotons survived,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1833810,
    "dDurationMs": 3690,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and they came out slow enough\nto do experiments with them."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1837500,
    "dDurationMs": 2008,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Of course, this was very inefficient."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1839508,
    "dDurationMs": 3002,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And so in 2015 and 2016,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1842510,
    "dDurationMs": 3203,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "a secondary ring called\nELENA was installed."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1845713,
    "dDurationMs": 4597,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "ELENA slows the antiprotons\nto 1.5% the speed of light,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1850310,
    "dDurationMs": 4233,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "a nice slow 16.2 million\nkilometers per hour."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1856610,
    "dDurationMs": 833,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This is running?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1857443,
    "dDurationMs": 3100,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- You are watching a\nlive antiproton machine."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1861380,
    "dDurationMs": 2550,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- Are the antiprotons going\naround in these circles?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1863930,
    "dDurationMs": 833,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- Exactly."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1864763,
    "dDurationMs": 2947,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The blue devices are\nmagnets, dipole magnets,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1867710,
    "dDurationMs": 2640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "which by Lorentz force\nmake the particles turn."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1870350,
    "dDurationMs": 1770,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Then you have the orange ones,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1872120,
    "dDurationMs": 1320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "which are quadrupole magnets,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1873440,
    "dDurationMs": 1860,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "which manage the focusing of this beam."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1875300,
    "dDurationMs": 1994,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "They're like lenses for particles."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1877294,
    "dDurationMs": 4305,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- It's a pretty thin pipe\nalmost that they go through."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1881599,
    "dDurationMs": 1831,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- Yeah, I mean you don't\nneed much there, right?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1883430,
    "dDurationMs": 1860,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Because as long as you\ndon't bend the particles,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1885290,
    "dDurationMs": 1530,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "they just want to go straight."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1886820,
    "dDurationMs": 1500,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "You need to keep good vacuum in there."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1888320,
    "dDurationMs": 3060,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Very good vacuum in fact.\nOtherwise they would annihilate."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1891380,
    "dDurationMs": 3359,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- And how often do you have\nannihilations in this loop?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1894739,
    "dDurationMs": 962,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- In here?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1895701,
    "dDurationMs": 1649,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- Yeah, because you can't\nhave a perfect vacuum."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1897350,
    "dDurationMs": 2790,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- Well, no, no, you have a bit of losses."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1900140,
    "dDurationMs": 2264,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But you know, the entire\nprocess of catching,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1902404,
    "dDurationMs": 3106,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "I mean from the moment\nof catching to the moment"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1905510,
    "dDurationMs": 1445,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of extraction to the experiments,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1906955,
    "dDurationMs": 4165,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "I think these days we\nare about 86% efficiency."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1911120,
    "dDurationMs": 2283,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "They have made it very efficient."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1913403,
    "dDurationMs": 1768,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- After the antiprotons\nhave been slowed down"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1915171,
    "dDurationMs": 3989,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "in ELENA, they are sent onto\nfive different experiments."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1919160,
    "dDurationMs": 2820,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Each of which is designed to\nstudy different properties"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1921980,
    "dDurationMs": 2066,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of antimatter to try and find ways"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1924046,
    "dDurationMs": 4069,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "in which antimatter behaves\ndifferently from normal matter."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1928115,
    "dDurationMs": 2715,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "One of the first\nexperiments that was done,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1930830,
    "dDurationMs": 3000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "which happened before the\nantimatter factory was built,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1933830,
    "dDurationMs": 3360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "was testing whether the mass\nof a proton and antiproton"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1937190,
    "dDurationMs": 960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "are the same."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1938150,
    "dDurationMs": 3412,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But to do that, it brings us\nback to our original problem."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1941562,
    "dDurationMs": 1963,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "How do you store antimatter?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1943525,
    "dDurationMs": 3248,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The way they solved this\nproblem is pretty clever."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1946773,
    "dDurationMs": 4007,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "They started with a tube, which\nwas pumped down to a vacuum."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1950780,
    "dDurationMs": 2760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "A superconducting magnet\nsits around this tube,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1953540,
    "dDurationMs": 1800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and it creates a magnetic field"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1955340,
    "dDurationMs": 2788,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that confines charged\nparticles to the center."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1958128,
    "dDurationMs": 1292,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "At the same time,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1959420,
    "dDurationMs": 2820,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "electrodes generate electric\nfields that function"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1962240,
    "dDurationMs": 1560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "as end caps, preventing"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1963800,
    "dDurationMs": 2431,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the particles from escaping out the ends."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1966231,
    "dDurationMs": 3389,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The whole tube is then cooled\ndown to around 4 Kelvin,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1969620,
    "dDurationMs": 3330,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "or minus 269 degrees Celsius."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1972950,
    "dDurationMs": 2520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This causes almost all\nthe remaining particles"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1975470,
    "dDurationMs": 1680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to condense and freeze,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1977150,
    "dDurationMs": 3774,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "resulting in a vacuum pressure\ncomparable to outer space."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1980924,
    "dDurationMs": 2226,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So now, they could fill this tube"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1983150,
    "dDurationMs": 2100,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "with something like antiprotons."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1985250,
    "dDurationMs": 2677,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And once inside, those\nantiprotons have nothing"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1987927,
    "dDurationMs": 3233,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to annihilate with, and nowhere to go."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1991160,
    "dDurationMs": 1950,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "They are trapped."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1993110,
    "dDurationMs": 3660,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "They had just built a\nreal-life antimatter trap."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1996770,
    "dDurationMs": 2580,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The technical term for\nthis is a Penning trap,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1999350,
    "dDurationMs": 3990,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "after Frans Penning, whose\nwork inspired the first one."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2003340,
    "dDurationMs": 3399,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Fittingly, the team that did\nthis at CERN was called TRAP."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2006739,
    "dDurationMs": 2271,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "With the antiprotons trapped,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2009010,
    "dDurationMs": 3188,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "they measured the charge-to-mass\nratio of the antiproton"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2012198,
    "dDurationMs": 2704,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and compared it to that of the proton."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2014902,
    "dDurationMs": 4519,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And they found it was equal\nto one part in 10 billion."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2019421,
    "dDurationMs": 3869,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Now, the Penning traps made\nstudying antimatter much easier."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2023290,
    "dDurationMs": 2445,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And so, it became a key tool\nthat the other experiments"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2025735,
    "dDurationMs": 2295,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "at the factory adopted."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2028030,
    "dDurationMs": 3570,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "In 2017, the base experiment\nused it to measure"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2031600,
    "dDurationMs": 2220,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the antiproton's magnetic moment."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2033820,
    "dDurationMs": 2670,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And they found that, within\ntheir level of accuracy,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2036490,
    "dDurationMs": 3960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "it was equal and opposite\nto that of the proton."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2040450,
    "dDurationMs": 4200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So, thus far, everything was\nbehaving just as predicted."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2044650,
    "dDurationMs": 3570,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But there is one force that\nthey hadn't directly probed yet."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2048220,
    "dDurationMs": 1920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Gravity. Gravity."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2050140,
    "dDurationMs": 2220,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Could that be part of the solution?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2052360,
    "dDurationMs": 1890,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- It very likely will be, ultimately."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2054250,
    "dDurationMs": 4140,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Part of why is because gravity\ndoes not obey the rules"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2058390,
    "dDurationMs": 2430,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of special relativity,\nwhich means it doesn't"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2060820,
    "dDurationMs": 3690,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "have to obey the CPT theorem\nlike the CERN model does."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2064510,
    "dDurationMs": 960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And so, in principle,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2065470,
    "dDurationMs": 1075,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that's an area"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2066545,
    "dDurationMs": 5000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "within which one could more\nnaturally expect larger values"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2071590,
    "dDurationMs": 2670,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of violations of C and CP and so on,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2074260,
    "dDurationMs": 2040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "or even a CPT altogether."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2076300,
    "dDurationMs": 1770,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- In fact, back in the 1950s,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2078070,
    "dDurationMs": 3150,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "a few physicists entertained\nthe idea of antigravity,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2081220,
    "dDurationMs": 2880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that antimatter would be\ngravitationally repulsive."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2084100,
    "dDurationMs": 1650,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So, while matter falls down"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2085750,
    "dDurationMs": 1593,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "in the Earth's gravitational field,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2087343,
    "dDurationMs": 1797,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "antimatter would rise up."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2089140,
    "dDurationMs": 2310,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- If you had a basketball\nmade of antimatter,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2091450,
    "dDurationMs": 930,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that would be easy to test."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2092380,
    "dDurationMs": 1350,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But getting a basketball of antimatter"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2093730,
    "dDurationMs": 1914,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "without it blowing up\non you is pretty hard."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2095644,
    "dDurationMs": 1166,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So..."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2097840,
    "dDurationMs": 1350,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It's not an easy thing"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2099190,
    "dDurationMs": 3060,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to do gravity experiments on particles."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2102250,
    "dDurationMs": 2970,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- You can't just drop an\nantiproton and see if it falls."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2105220,
    "dDurationMs": 2490,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Because antiprotons\nare negatively charged."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2107710,
    "dDurationMs": 3180,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And the electric force is\nmuch stronger than gravity."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2110890,
    "dDurationMs": 2637,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So, even small stray electric\nfields would influence them"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2113527,
    "dDurationMs": 2403,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "way more than gravity would."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2115930,
    "dDurationMs": 2340,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So what you need is something neutral."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2118270,
    "dDurationMs": 5000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "What you need is an antiatom.\nSo you're making antiatoms?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2123580,
    "dDurationMs": 833,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- Yes."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2124413,
    "dDurationMs": 1147,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- How do you make the antiatom?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2125560,
    "dDurationMs": 5000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- So, what we do is we use\nantiprotons and positrons."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2131553,
    "dDurationMs": 3847,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Basically, we merge them.\nThey become antihydrogen."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2135400,
    "dDurationMs": 2880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- [Casper] Now, there are several\nways to make antihydrogen."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2138280,
    "dDurationMs": 2850,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And different experiments\ndo it in different ways."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2141130,
    "dDurationMs": 4099,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But for GBAR, it all starts\nhere, in this bunker."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2145229,
    "dDurationMs": 2771,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- [Patrice] In this bunker,\nwe have a small accelerator."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2148000,
    "dDurationMs": 3215,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So, we make ourselves our own positrons."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2151215,
    "dDurationMs": 4165,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And then we capture them in a trap here."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2155380,
    "dDurationMs": 2100,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- They accelerate a beam of electrons up"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2157480,
    "dDurationMs": 2910,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to 99.9% the speed of light,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2160390,
    "dDurationMs": 3210,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and then fire those at a tungsten target."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2163600,
    "dDurationMs": 2533,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Now, while tungsten itself\nis electrically neutral,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2166133,
    "dDurationMs": 3347,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "at the high speed those\nelectrons enter the tungsten,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2169480,
    "dDurationMs": 1860,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "they get close enough to the nuclei"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2171340,
    "dDurationMs": 2670,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that the electron cloud\ncan no longer screen"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2174010,
    "dDurationMs": 2550,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the intense positive charge within."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2176560,
    "dDurationMs": 3300,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Thus, these nuclei create\nstrong electric fields."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2179860,
    "dDurationMs": 2430,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And those fields then\nyank the electrons around,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2182290,
    "dDurationMs": 2250,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "causing them to rapidly decelerate,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2184540,
    "dDurationMs": 2447,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "as if they've just slammed on the brakes."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2186987,
    "dDurationMs": 3043,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But the thing is, when\nthese electrons break,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2190030,
    "dDurationMs": 2700,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "they lose energy by emitting photons."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2192730,
    "dDurationMs": 2040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The Germans have a great word for this."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2194770,
    "dDurationMs": 4170,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It's called Bremsstrahlung,\nor breaking radiation."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2198940,
    "dDurationMs": 2910,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This breaking radiation\nproduces a wide range"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2201850,
    "dDurationMs": 3750,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of photons, ranging from\nlow-energy X-rays all the way up"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2205600,
    "dDurationMs": 3365,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to nearly 9-megaelectronvolt gamma rays."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2208965,
    "dDurationMs": 2335,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Now, out of all of these photons,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2211300,
    "dDurationMs": 3240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "it's the gamma rays above\nroughly 1-megaelectronvolt"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2214540,
    "dDurationMs": 1650,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that are important."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2216190,
    "dDurationMs": 2477,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Because when one of these\ngamma rays passes close"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2218667,
    "dDurationMs": 2023,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to a tungsten nucleus,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2220690,
    "dDurationMs": 2670,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "there's a chance that it\ntransfers its momentum"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2223360,
    "dDurationMs": 2490,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to that nucleus and\nconverts all its energy"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2225850,
    "dDurationMs": 1860,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "into the mass and kinetic energy"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2227710,
    "dDurationMs": 2700,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of an electron-positron pair."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2230410,
    "dDurationMs": 3000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But unfortunately, this\nisn't a clean process"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2233410,
    "dDurationMs": 2630,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that just makes electron-positron pairs."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2236040,
    "dDurationMs": 2740,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- It produces positrons,\nbut it also produces a lot"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2238780,
    "dDurationMs": 2580,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of photons, gamma rays, neutrons."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2241360,
    "dDurationMs": 2400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And these are deadly."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2243760,
    "dDurationMs": 3390,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And that particle mess\ncreates two problems."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2247150,
    "dDurationMs": 2490,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The first is that deadly radiation."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2249640,
    "dDurationMs": 833,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- It's supposed to be one"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2250473,
    "dDurationMs": 4777,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of the highest, strongest\nsource of radiation at CERN."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2255250,
    "dDurationMs": 2580,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- This is one of the highest?\n- Yes."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2257830,
    "dDurationMs": 4680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "If you enter while it is\nworking, you die in 10 seconds."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2262510,
    "dDurationMs": 2100,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- You die in 10 seconds?\n- You cannot escape."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2264610,
    "dDurationMs": 2257,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- It's terrifying.\n- You melt from inside."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2266867,
    "dDurationMs": 2363,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- You melt from inside..."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2269230,
    "dDurationMs": 2850,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "You're saying that way\ntoo casually. (laughs)"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2272080,
    "dDurationMs": 2310,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And the second problem\nis that what comes out"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2274390,
    "dDurationMs": 3517,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of the tungsten isn't a nice,\nuniform beam of positrons."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2277907,
    "dDurationMs": 3773,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Instead, you get a shower\nof electrons, neutrons,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2281680,
    "dDurationMs": 2850,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "positrons and photons all mixed together,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2284530,
    "dDurationMs": 3604,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "all traveling at different\nangles and different speeds."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2288134,
    "dDurationMs": 2726,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The first problem is solved by encasing"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2290860,
    "dDurationMs": 3420,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the entire setup with\nmassive 1.2-meter thick,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2294280,
    "dDurationMs": 3993,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "67% concrete and 33% iron blocks."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2299980,
    "dDurationMs": 1800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And this is enough to shield us?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2301780,
    "dDurationMs": 1665,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- Yes.\n- Because it's photons?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2303445,
    "dDurationMs": 4065,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- Yes. This is 1,400 tons."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2307510,
    "dDurationMs": 833,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- Okay."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2308343,
    "dDurationMs": 2557,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Okay, I feel a bit better\nnow. Is it running now?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2310900,
    "dDurationMs": 833,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- No."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2311733,
    "dDurationMs": 3577,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But even if it runs, we can\nsit just outside and it's okay."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2315310,
    "dDurationMs": 2700,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- Okay, so we're safe. You wear your..."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2318010,
    "dDurationMs": 1903,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- Your badge, the dosimeter."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2319913,
    "dDurationMs": 960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- Okay, so you would know?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2320873,
    "dDurationMs": 986,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- Yeah."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2321859,
    "dDurationMs": 1095,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- But I guess 10 seconds, not..."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2322954,
    "dDurationMs": 1200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- Too late.\n- Too late."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2325180,
    "dDurationMs": 2880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Solving the second problem\nis a little more involved."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2328060,
    "dDurationMs": 2910,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And it's honestly one of\nthe coolest combinations"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2330970,
    "dDurationMs": 2970,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of physics and engineering\nI've ever come across."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2333940,
    "dDurationMs": 1440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So, strap in."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2335380,
    "dDurationMs": 2520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "When the positrons leave\nthe tungsten target,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2337900,
    "dDurationMs": 2430,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "some are traveling at\na few percent the speed"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2340330,
    "dDurationMs": 3123,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of light, while others are\ntraveling at more than 90%"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2343453,
    "dDurationMs": 1647,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the speed of light."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2345100,
    "dDurationMs": 3000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Now, this massive spread makes\nit very hard to work with."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2348100,
    "dDurationMs": 4620,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So we need to slow them down\nto around 0.34% the speed"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2352720,
    "dDurationMs": 4361,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of light, or around 3.7\nmillion kilometers per hour."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2357081,
    "dDurationMs": 3109,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The way they do this is kind of crazy,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2360190,
    "dDurationMs": 2370,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "because they shoot the\npositrons, remember,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2362560,
    "dDurationMs": 1991,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "those are antiparticles, at a mesh"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2364551,
    "dDurationMs": 5000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of ultra-fine 20-micrometer\ndiameter tungsten wires, which,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2369670,
    "dDurationMs": 2204,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of course, are made of normal matter."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2371874,
    "dDurationMs": 3209,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "When a fast positron\nenters the tungsten wire,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2375083,
    "dDurationMs": 3377,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "it immediately loses energy\ndue to scattering off"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2378460,
    "dDurationMs": 1276,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the tungsten atoms."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2379736,
    "dDurationMs": 2084,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And this happens so fast"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2381820,
    "dDurationMs": 2820,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that within around 10\npicoseconds, that is,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2384640,
    "dDurationMs": 1645,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "10 trillionths of a second,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2386285,
    "dDurationMs": 3575,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the positron has slowed down\nto match the thermal energy"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2389860,
    "dDurationMs": 873,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of the tungsten."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2391720,
    "dDurationMs": 3300,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But now, the positron is\nstill trapped inside the wire."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2395020,
    "dDurationMs": 1200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So, from here on,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2396220,
    "dDurationMs": 2760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "through a random walk of\ncollisions and scattering,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2398980,
    "dDurationMs": 2160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "it needs to find its way out."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2401140,
    "dDurationMs": 2520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And if it bumps into an\nelectron or gets stuck"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2403660,
    "dDurationMs": 3330,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "in a defect, it never makes it out."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2406990,
    "dDurationMs": 2910,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So you might expect almost\nnone of these positrons"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2409900,
    "dDurationMs": 833,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to make it out."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2410733,
    "dDurationMs": 1237,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And for almost all"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2411970,
    "dDurationMs": 3390,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of them to find an\nelectron and annihilate."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2415360,
    "dDurationMs": 1620,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And you'd be right."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2416980,
    "dDurationMs": 2790,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The efficiency of this\nprocess is terrible."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2419770,
    "dDurationMs": 3090,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "For every thousand fast\npositrons entering the mesh,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2422860,
    "dDurationMs": 4036,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "only about one comes out\nas a usable slow positron."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2426896,
    "dDurationMs": 3164,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Another problem is that these\npositrons don't come out"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2430060,
    "dDurationMs": 2340,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "as a nice organized beam."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2432400,
    "dDurationMs": 3180,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Instead, they are emitted\nat all kinds of angles."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2435580,
    "dDurationMs": 2820,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So we need to find a way to focus them."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2438400,
    "dDurationMs": 2670,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This is done by letting\nthe shower of particles go"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2441070,
    "dDurationMs": 3090,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "through a solenoid, which\nis a long coiled wire"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2444160,
    "dDurationMs": 1860,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "with a current running through."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2446020,
    "dDurationMs": 2970,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "That current creates a\nmagnetic field inside the coil"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2448990,
    "dDurationMs": 3768,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that acts as a magnetic lens\nand focuses the positrons."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2452758,
    "dDurationMs": 3042,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This lets us capture many\nof the positrons emitted"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2455800,
    "dDurationMs": 2913,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "at wide angles that\nwould otherwise be lost."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2459580,
    "dDurationMs": 2190,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But right now we still have a mix"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2461770,
    "dDurationMs": 3390,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of positrons, electrons,\nneutrons and photons."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2465160,
    "dDurationMs": 2850,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So the next step is to separate these."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2468010,
    "dDurationMs": 2524,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "To do this, we use another magnetic field."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2470534,
    "dDurationMs": 3626,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This curves the electrons\none way into a beam dump."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2474160,
    "dDurationMs": 1380,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The photons and neutrons,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2475540,
    "dDurationMs": 2820,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "because they have no electric\ncharge, are unaffected,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2478360,
    "dDurationMs": 3205,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "so they go straight through\nand are absorbed by shielding."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2481565,
    "dDurationMs": 2838,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And the positrons, because\nof their positive charge,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2484403,
    "dDurationMs": 2837,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "curve the opposite way to electrons."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2487240,
    "dDurationMs": 3090,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And they go on to the next stage."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2490330,
    "dDurationMs": 3300,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Now we're left with a\nbeam of just positrons."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2493630,
    "dDurationMs": 1140,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The only issue"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2494770,
    "dDurationMs": 2250,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "is that because of the terrible efficiency"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2497020,
    "dDurationMs": 1503,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "from slowing down those positrons,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2498523,
    "dDurationMs": 2920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "each single shot only generates around"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2501443,
    "dDurationMs": 3227,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "1,000 usable slow positrons."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2504670,
    "dDurationMs": 3360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But we need millions or even\nbillions of slow positrons"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2508030,
    "dDurationMs": 1860,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "for the next stage."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2509890,
    "dDurationMs": 2970,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So the solution is to\naccumulate the positrons"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2512860,
    "dDurationMs": 1770,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "in a particle trap,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2514630,
    "dDurationMs": 3120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "where over several minutes\nit builds up a positron cloud"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2517750,
    "dDurationMs": 4530,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of around 100 million or more\npositrons which is enough"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2522280,
    "dDurationMs": 1023,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "for the next stage."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2524140,
    "dDurationMs": 1980,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- I said you merge\npositrons and antiprotons,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2526120,
    "dDurationMs": 1620,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but we do even more complicated."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2527740,
    "dDurationMs": 2697,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "First we make positronium.\nPositronium is a..."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2530437,
    "dDurationMs": 2403,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- Positronium?\n- Yes."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2532840,
    "dDurationMs": 1410,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- [Casper] Positronium is an electron"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2534250,
    "dDurationMs": 2280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and a positron orbiting each other like"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2536530,
    "dDurationMs": 1950,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "a binary star system."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2538480,
    "dDurationMs": 2388,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It's an exotic form of\nmatter and it only lasts"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2540868,
    "dDurationMs": 3792,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "about one tenth to 142 nanoseconds,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2544660,
    "dDurationMs": 3044,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "before the two come\ntogether and annihilate."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2547704,
    "dDurationMs": 3166,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The way they make this is by\nusing strong magnetic fields"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2550870,
    "dDurationMs": 2604,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to compress the cloud\nof positrons and fire it"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2553474,
    "dDurationMs": 3186,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "at porous silicon dioxide films."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2556660,
    "dDurationMs": 2070,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "When these positrons enter these films,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2558730,
    "dDurationMs": 2190,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "they rip away electrons from their atoms."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2560920,
    "dDurationMs": 2670,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And some of those electrons\nthen bind with positrons"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2563590,
    "dDurationMs": 1230,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to form positronium."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2564820,
    "dDurationMs": 3090,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And then a part of that\npositronium diffuses out"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2567910,
    "dDurationMs": 3090,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of the films into the\nvacuum of the next stage,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2571000,
    "dDurationMs": 4680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the interaction chamber, where\nit's time for the final step."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2575680,
    "dDurationMs": 3690,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- So this is where, we prepare this here."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2579370,
    "dDurationMs": 2130,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- That's the positronium?\n- Yes."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2581500,
    "dDurationMs": 1980,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- That's crazy.\n- We send antiprotons"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2583480,
    "dDurationMs": 2532,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to the positronium where\nit makes antihydrogen."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2586012,
    "dDurationMs": 2718,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- [Casper] Now, since\npositronium only survives"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2588730,
    "dDurationMs": 4950,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "for about 142 nanoseconds, this\nneeds to be timed perfectly."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2593680,
    "dDurationMs": 960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- So if you want"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2594640,
    "dDurationMs": 2790,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to see where we catch the antiprotons..."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2597430,
    "dDurationMs": 833,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- Yes, I would love"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2598263,
    "dDurationMs": 1987,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to see where you catch the antiprotons."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2600250,
    "dDurationMs": 4590,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "I was not expecting to get\nthis close. It's right here?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2604840,
    "dDurationMs": 1230,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- This."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2606070,
    "dDurationMs": 3750,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- That's awesome. So we\nget the antiprotons here..."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2609820,
    "dDurationMs": 2340,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- Yes.\n- And then what happens?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2612160,
    "dDurationMs": 3022,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- So it goes there inside this box."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2615182,
    "dDurationMs": 1008,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- [Casper] Yeah."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2616190,
    "dDurationMs": 2699,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- Inside the box it will\nmeet the positronium."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2618889,
    "dDurationMs": 2154,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- There meets the positronium."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2621043,
    "dDurationMs": 2637,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Kind of scared, honestly."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2623680,
    "dDurationMs": 1923,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It sounds like there's music in here."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2626500,
    "dDurationMs": 2490,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "As the positronium enters\nthe interaction chamber,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2628990,
    "dDurationMs": 2190,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the antiproton beam needs to be fired"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2631180,
    "dDurationMs": 1721,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "through at that exact moment."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2632901,
    "dDurationMs": 3469,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "When done correctly, around\nthree million antiprotons"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2636370,
    "dDurationMs": 2430,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "or so pass through the positronium."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2638800,
    "dDurationMs": 1110,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "If all goes well,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2639910,
    "dDurationMs": 4108,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "around one to a few of those\nantiprotons steal a positron"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2644018,
    "dDurationMs": 3249,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to create an atom of antihydrogen."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2648597,
    "dDurationMs": 2443,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Okay, so we've got positrons\ncoming through here,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2651040,
    "dDurationMs": 1152,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "all the way through here."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2652192,
    "dDurationMs": 921,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This is where you capture the positrons..."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2653113,
    "dDurationMs": 2727,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- Yes, we accumulate them.\n- You accumulate them."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2655840,
    "dDurationMs": 833,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And then you shoot them"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2656673,
    "dDurationMs": 1936,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "through there and you\nmake the positronium."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2658609,
    "dDurationMs": 3261,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And then you shoot that into\nthat chamber so it mixes"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2661870,
    "dDurationMs": 1111,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "with the antiprotons."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2662981,
    "dDurationMs": 2459,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- Yep.\n- It's so cool."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2665440,
    "dDurationMs": 5000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It's so cool. Right in here\nis where they make antiatoms."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2670511,
    "dDurationMs": 1259,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Antihydrogen."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2671770,
    "dDurationMs": 3503,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "They shoot the antiprotons\nthrough and they capture,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2675273,
    "dDurationMs": 3997,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "they capture those antielectrons\nto form antihydrogen."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2679270,
    "dDurationMs": 2760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Which then travels through\nhere and then, you know,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2682030,
    "dDurationMs": 833,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "it will go all"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2682863,
    "dDurationMs": 3247,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the way along there and\nthey do their experiments."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2686110,
    "dDurationMs": 1140,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It's absolutely insane."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2687250,
    "dDurationMs": 3930,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "I feel like I should not be\nin here, but it's so cool."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2691180,
    "dDurationMs": 4410,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Now, one question I had after\nlearning all of this is, why?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2695590,
    "dDurationMs": 1560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "I mean, why do this?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2697150,
    "dDurationMs": 3237,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Because the ALPHA-g experiment\ncan already make 100"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2700387,
    "dDurationMs": 3003,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "antihydrogen atoms in four hours using"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2703390,
    "dDurationMs": 2070,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "a much simpler process."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2705460,
    "dDurationMs": 3233,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So why is the GBAR team\nspending years to build"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2708693,
    "dDurationMs": 3277,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "a particle accelerator,\na positronium converter,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2711970,
    "dDurationMs": 2002,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and a way to shoot the antiprotons"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2713972,
    "dDurationMs": 2168,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "through this positronium just"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2716140,
    "dDurationMs": 3926,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to make fewer antihydrogen\natoms in a slower"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2720066,
    "dDurationMs": 1894,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and more difficult way?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2721960,
    "dDurationMs": 1950,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Especially when you consider"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2723910,
    "dDurationMs": 4020,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that in 2023 ALPHA-g\ndid its own test to see"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2727930,
    "dDurationMs": 2700,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "whether antihydrogen falls up or down."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2730630,
    "dDurationMs": 1830,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Well, to understand why,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2732460,
    "dDurationMs": 3840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "we need to understand exactly\nwhat it is that ALPHA-g did."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2736300,
    "dDurationMs": 2880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Their setup works something like this."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2739180,
    "dDurationMs": 1290,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Positrons are created"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2740470,
    "dDurationMs": 2181,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "by a radioactive source, accumulated,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2742651,
    "dDurationMs": 2524,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and are then injected up and trapped."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2745175,
    "dDurationMs": 3545,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Antiprotons that come in\nfrom ELENA are accumulated"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2748720,
    "dDurationMs": 2580,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "in a trap and then also injected in a trap"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2751300,
    "dDurationMs": 2345,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that sits just below the positrons."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2753645,
    "dDurationMs": 3865,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Next, the two antiparticle\nclouds are gently merged."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2757510,
    "dDurationMs": 2460,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This causes some of the\nantiprotons to capture"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2759970,
    "dDurationMs": 2691,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "a positron and form antihydrogen."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2762661,
    "dDurationMs": 2439,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Now, antihydrogen is neutral,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2765100,
    "dDurationMs": 2880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "which means that the Penning\ntrap can no longer hold it."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2767980,
    "dDurationMs": 1800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So if nothing else was done,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2769780,
    "dDurationMs": 2425,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the antihydrogen atoms\nwould form, drift off,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2772205,
    "dDurationMs": 4265,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and within microseconds\nannihilate at one of the walls."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2776470,
    "dDurationMs": 1950,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It would all be for nothing."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2778420,
    "dDurationMs": 2040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And this is exactly what happened"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2780460,
    "dDurationMs": 2280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "with the earliest\nantihydrogen experiments."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2782740,
    "dDurationMs": 1592,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "They couldn't hold on to it."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2784332,
    "dDurationMs": 3508,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Fortunately, there is a\nway to trap antihydrogen,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2787840,
    "dDurationMs": 2280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "because it has a small magnetic moment."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2790120,
    "dDurationMs": 3090,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So a second magnetic trap\nwas engineered around"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2793210,
    "dDurationMs": 2880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the device, which could\ncapture the antihydrogen."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2796090,
    "dDurationMs": 2490,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Unfortunately, that trap is pretty weak,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2798580,
    "dDurationMs": 3450,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "so most antihydrogen atoms\nescape and annihilate."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2802030,
    "dDurationMs": 3600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But a few stay. And the\nidea then is simple."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2805630,
    "dDurationMs": 2640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Slowly weaken the magnetic\nfield holding them,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2808270,
    "dDurationMs": 2370,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and as the trap gets weaker and weaker,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2810640,
    "dDurationMs": 1980,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "antiatoms start to escape."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2812620,
    "dDurationMs": 3450,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And if gravity pulls antimatter\ndown, like normal matter,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2816070,
    "dDurationMs": 2460,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "then more atoms should\nescape through the bottom"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2818530,
    "dDurationMs": 1500,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "than through the top."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2820030,
    "dDurationMs": 4149,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So what did they find? Does\nantimatter fall up or down?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2824179,
    "dDurationMs": 3201,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "They found that antimatter falls down."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2827380,
    "dDurationMs": 3690,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So it rules out any exotic\ntheories of antigravity."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2831070,
    "dDurationMs": 3690,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "They measured the gravitational\nacceleration as 75%"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2834760,
    "dDurationMs": 4722,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of normal gravity, plus\nminus 13%, plus minus 16%."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2839482,
    "dDurationMs": 3168,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Which is possibly consistent\nwith normal gravity,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2842650,
    "dDurationMs": 2610,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but of course the error bars are huge."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2845260,
    "dDurationMs": 2700,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And this is also why GBAR is so important."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2847960,
    "dDurationMs": 1500,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Because their hope is to get"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2849460,
    "dDurationMs": 2670,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the measurement accuracy down to 1%,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2852130,
    "dDurationMs": 3510,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and ultimately to 1 in 100,000."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2855640,
    "dDurationMs": 2128,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "See, when you're doing\na gravity experiment"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2857768,
    "dDurationMs": 1682,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "on atoms like this,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2859450,
    "dDurationMs": 2970,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "you want those atoms to\nbe as still as possible"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2862420,
    "dDurationMs": 1020,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "before you drop them."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2863440,
    "dDurationMs": 4020,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "In other words, you want them\nto be as cold as possible."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2867460,
    "dDurationMs": 3870,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Now, ALPHA-g can get really\ncold to about 0.5 Kelvin,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2871330,
    "dDurationMs": 2970,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "which is half a degree\nabove absolute zero."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2874300,
    "dDurationMs": 2760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But GBAR wants to bring\nthis way down to less"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2877060,
    "dDurationMs": 4413,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "than 10 micro-Kelvin, that\nis 50,000 times colder."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2882700,
    "dDurationMs": 2880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The way they plan on\ndoing this is actually not"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2885580,
    "dDurationMs": 1980,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "by making antihydrogen atoms,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2887560,
    "dDurationMs": 3060,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but by making an antihydrogen ion,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2890620,
    "dDurationMs": 2710,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "one antiproton and two positrons."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2893330,
    "dDurationMs": 4010,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The hope is that once an\nantihydrogen atom has formed,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2897340,
    "dDurationMs": 2550,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "it runs into a second positronium atom"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2899890,
    "dDurationMs": 2010,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and steals another positron."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2901900,
    "dDurationMs": 1860,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "At first, that might seem strange,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2903760,
    "dDurationMs": 2605,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "because now we're back to\nhaving a charged particle."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2906365,
    "dDurationMs": 1355,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And as we learned,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2907720,
    "dDurationMs": 2430,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "you can just drop a charged\nparticle and measure"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2910150,
    "dDurationMs": 1770,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the effects of gravity."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2911920,
    "dDurationMs": 1320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But charged particles"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2913240,
    "dDurationMs": 2580,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "are actually much easier to trap and cool."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2915820,
    "dDurationMs": 1470,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And we can use that."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2917290,
    "dDurationMs": 1410,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Because now it can be held"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2918700,
    "dDurationMs": 2610,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "in a much stronger electromagnetic trap."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2921310,
    "dDurationMs": 2670,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And once there, you can inject ultra-cold,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2923980,
    "dDurationMs": 2580,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "like 10 millikelvin, beryllium ions"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2926560,
    "dDurationMs": 1980,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that have been laser-cooled."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2928540,
    "dDurationMs": 2761,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The antihydrogen ion then\nbounces around and collides"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2931301,
    "dDurationMs": 1829,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "with these beryllium ions,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2933130,
    "dDurationMs": 2494,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "slowly transferring its\nkinetic energy to them"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2935624,
    "dDurationMs": 1916,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and thus cooling down."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2937540,
    "dDurationMs": 1500,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And they won't annihilate,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2939040,
    "dDurationMs": 2760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "because both particles\nare positively charged,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2941800,
    "dDurationMs": 1550,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "so they repel each other."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2943350,
    "dDurationMs": 2050,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Then you keep cooling down"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2945400,
    "dDurationMs": 3150,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the beryllium ions using\nmore advanced techniques,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2948550,
    "dDurationMs": 2490,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "until you hit the micro-Kelvin range."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2951040,
    "dDurationMs": 2850,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And this is ultimately\nhow they hope to reach"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2953890,
    "dDurationMs": 2403,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "a temperature of around 10 micro-Kelvin."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2957550,
    "dDurationMs": 3660,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Now, with the antihydrogen\nion as still as possible,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2961210,
    "dDurationMs": 1950,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "they shoot a laser pulse at it,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2963160,
    "dDurationMs": 2686,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "dislodging one of its\npositrons and resulting"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2965846,
    "dDurationMs": 3284,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "in a neutral antihydrogen atom."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2969130,
    "dDurationMs": 1140,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And as a result,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2970270,
    "dDurationMs": 2430,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the electromagnetic trap\ncan no longer hold it."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2972700,
    "dDurationMs": 3990,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And so it falls. Around 20 centimeters."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2976690,
    "dDurationMs": 2400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "At that temperature\nand over that distance,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2979090,
    "dDurationMs": 2550,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "you can time the fall\nprecisely enough to measure"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2981640,
    "dDurationMs": 3233,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the gravitational\nacceleration to about 1%."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2985720,
    "dDurationMs": 1320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So all of this,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2987040,
    "dDurationMs": 2481,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the particle accelerator\nmaking the positronium,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2989521,
    "dDurationMs": 2439,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and then the hard way of cooling it,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2991960,
    "dDurationMs": 1230,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "all of it is just to watch"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2993190,
    "dDurationMs": 3244,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "a single antiatom fall 20 centimeters."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2996434,
    "dDurationMs": 3086,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Because this process is the only known way"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2999520,
    "dDurationMs": 1626,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to make antihydrogen ions."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 3001146,
    "dDurationMs": 2394,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And using those ions is the only way"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 3003540,
    "dDurationMs": 2700,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to get antimatter cold enough to perform"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 3006240,
    "dDurationMs": 1797,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "an accurate enough experiment."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 3008037,
    "dDurationMs": 2943,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Now, they haven't managed to do this yet."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 3010980,
    "dDurationMs": 2610,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So far, they've only made antihydrogen."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 3013590,
    "dDurationMs": 1590,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But if they can manage,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 3015180,
    "dDurationMs": 2430,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "then it would be the\nmost precise measurement"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 3017610,
    "dDurationMs": 1890,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of antimatter under gravity."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 3019500,
    "dDurationMs": 2763,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Although this is likely still years away."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 3023520,
    "dDurationMs": 3120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Now, one thing that makes\nthis research so tricky"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 3026640,
    "dDurationMs": 2700,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and also relatively slow is that there"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 3029340,
    "dDurationMs": 2370,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "is only one antimatter\nfactory in the world."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 3031710,
    "dDurationMs": 1339,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And so the number of places"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 3033049,
    "dDurationMs": 3731,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that can study real\nantimatter is very limited."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 3036780,
    "dDurationMs": 1530,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But that might soon change,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 3038310,
    "dDurationMs": 4020,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "all thanks to another\nexperiment at the factory."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 3042330,
    "dDurationMs": 2460,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The BASE experiment was built to measure"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 3044790,
    "dDurationMs": 2193,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the magnetic moment of the antiproton."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 3046983,
    "dDurationMs": 2157,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "If CPT symmetry holds,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 3049140,
    "dDurationMs": 2468,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "then it should be exactly\nequal and opposite"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 3051608,
    "dDurationMs": 1852,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to that of the proton."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 3053460,
    "dDurationMs": 2310,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But they kept running into a problem."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 3055770,
    "dDurationMs": 2430,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- CERN has continuously\nramping magnetic fields"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 3058200,
    "dDurationMs": 1800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "in the background.\n- Right."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 3060000,
    "dDurationMs": 2250,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Even though these fluctuations were tiny,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 3062250,
    "dDurationMs": 1950,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "around 20,000 times weaker"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 3064200,
    "dDurationMs": 1359,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "than the Earth's magnetic field,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 3065559,
    "dDurationMs": 3681,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "at the precision BASE was\nworking at, they hit a wall."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 3069240,
    "dDurationMs": 3690,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- The only concept basically to overcome"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 3072930,
    "dDurationMs": 2220,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "this problem is to move the particles out"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 3075150,
    "dDurationMs": 1620,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of the accelerator."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 3076770,
    "dDurationMs": 1830,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- So they built a Penning trap"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 3078600,
    "dDurationMs": 2910,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "with its own power supply,\nits own cooling system,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 3081510,
    "dDurationMs": 2013,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and two storage holes for antiprotons."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 3084360,
    "dDurationMs": 2513,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So now they could fill those\nholes with antiprotons,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 3086873,
    "dDurationMs": 3513,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "store them, and carry them\nto wherever they wanted."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 3090386,
    "dDurationMs": 1046,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "They just created"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 3091432,
    "dDurationMs": 4031,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the world's first\nportable antimatter trap."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 3096354,
    "dDurationMs": 4146,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So of course I asked them a\npressing scientific question."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 3100500,
    "dDurationMs": 2190,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Are you gonna make it\nlook super futuristic?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 3102690,
    "dDurationMs": 1285,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Because it's got to be"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 3103975,
    "dDurationMs": 4488,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the most badass transport\ncontainer ever made."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 3108463,
    "dDurationMs": 3617,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- I just have this trap here in my office."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 3112080,
    "dDurationMs": 1624,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Maybe I can show it to you."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 3113704,
    "dDurationMs": 1346,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- Oh, yes, please. Oh..."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 3115050,
    "dDurationMs": 1620,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- This is one of these Penning traps."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 3116670,
    "dDurationMs": 2430,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And they are inside the\nsuperconducting magnet."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 3119100,
    "dDurationMs": 4230,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So the heavy part is basically\nthe superconducting magnet."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 3123330,
    "dDurationMs": 1719,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But these are these trap electrodes."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 3125049,
    "dDurationMs": 1701,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- And it works."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 3126750,
    "dDurationMs": 1800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "They have cracked the code of storing"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 3128550,
    "dDurationMs": 2721,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the most volatile\nsubstance in the universe."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 3131271,
    "dDurationMs": 4929,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Their current record for\nstoring antiprotons is 614 days."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 3136200,
    "dDurationMs": 2730,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "That is, they can store\nantimatter, you know,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 3138930,
    "dDurationMs": 3060,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the stuff that annihilates\nas soon as it touches matter,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 3141990,
    "dDurationMs": 1950,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "for close to two years."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 3143940,
    "dDurationMs": 1560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "That is absurd."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 3145500,
    "dDurationMs": 2220,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- This is this antiproton reservoir trap"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 3147720,
    "dDurationMs": 4590,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that stores antiprotons for\nlonger than one or two years."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 3152310,
    "dDurationMs": 3090,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- That's awesome. But\nhere's what that means."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 3155400,
    "dDurationMs": 3780,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Because if you can store\nantimatter for years in a box,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 3159180,
    "dDurationMs": 4532,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and you can put the box on a\ntruck, then why not ship it?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 3163712,
    "dDurationMs": 4018,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- We can start distributing antiprotons"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 3167730,
    "dDurationMs": 2370,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to ambitious experiments\nall around the planet."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 3170100,
    "dDurationMs": 3570,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And everyone who has a\ngood idea what we could do"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 3173670,
    "dDurationMs": 3360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "with these particles\nwill get these particles."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 3177030,
    "dDurationMs": 1950,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- I'm just imagining this map in my head"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 3178980,
    "dDurationMs": 2100,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "where you have the big antimatter factory,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 3181080,
    "dDurationMs": 2580,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and then it's gonna be\nsending antimatter all"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 3183660,
    "dDurationMs": 3660,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "over the world to all the\ntop research institutions."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 3187320,
    "dDurationMs": 2100,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- That's great, right?\n- It's awesome."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 3189420,
    "dDurationMs": 1860,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- Fantastic solution.\n- Fantastic. Yeah."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 3191280,
    "dDurationMs": 3750,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- Yes, yes, yes.\n- And they've already started."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 3195030,
    "dDurationMs": 2627,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "On the 24th of March, 2026,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 3197657,
    "dDurationMs": 3343,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "a crane lifted an 800-kilogram trap out"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 3201000,
    "dDurationMs": 3840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of the antimatter factory\nand loaded it onto a truck,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 3204840,
    "dDurationMs": 3510,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "which then drove on a\n10-kilometer loop around CERN."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 3208350,
    "dDurationMs": 3813,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And it was filled with 92 antiprotons."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 3213150,
    "dDurationMs": 1920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So perhaps \"Angels and Demons\""
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 3215070,
    "dDurationMs": 2160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "wasn't that far off after all."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 3217230,
    "dDurationMs": 967,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "In the near future,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 3218197,
    "dDurationMs": 3323,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "there could be actual\nboxes of antimatter that,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 3221520,
    "dDurationMs": 2208,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "at least in theory, could be stolen."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 3223728,
    "dDurationMs": 2592,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So does that also mean\nthat they were right"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 3226320,
    "dDurationMs": 2640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "about that one eighth\nof a gram of antimatter?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 3228960,
    "dDurationMs": 3150,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Well, we wanted to find\nout, so we tested it."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 3232110,
    "dDurationMs": 2100,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "I mean, we simulated it."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 3234210,
    "dDurationMs": 3750,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- This is the most supervillain\ncall I've ever got. (laughs)"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 3237960,
    "dDurationMs": 2290,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- I'm really getting\ninto my villain arc here."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 3240250,
    "dDurationMs": 5000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Okay, so let's find our\npoor target, Vatican City."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 3246030,
    "dDurationMs": 2490,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "We've got an eighth of a gram, you know,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 3248520,
    "dDurationMs": 2550,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "selected right there, 0.125."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 3251070,
    "dDurationMs": 1440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Who wants to do a countdown?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 3252510,
    "dDurationMs": 3473,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- Three, two, one. Let's go!"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 3257463,
    "dDurationMs": 917,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- Let's go!"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 3259421,
    "dDurationMs": 989,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- Oh my God."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 3260410,
    "dDurationMs": 3500,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- Okay, so we've got a few\nlevels of destruction here."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 3263910,
    "dDurationMs": 1620,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "We've got the fireball."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 3265530,
    "dDurationMs": 2310,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This is just all instantly vaporized."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 3267840,
    "dDurationMs": 3238,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It's turned into pure\nplasma, which is insane."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 3271078,
    "dDurationMs": 1862,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- Oh, St. Peter's Basilica."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 3272940,
    "dDurationMs": 1440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- It's got a temperature"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 3274380,
    "dDurationMs": 2850,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of about 100 million degrees Celsius,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 3277230,
    "dDurationMs": 2250,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "which is, you know, pretty chill."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 3279480,
    "dDurationMs": 4507,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "You can see it released\nabout 2.25 times 10"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 3283987,
    "dDurationMs": 5000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to the 13 joules, or I guess\nabout 22 trillion joules,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 3289830,
    "dDurationMs": 5000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "which is the equivalent of like\n36% of the Hiroshima blast."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 3295440,
    "dDurationMs": 3150,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "If we zoom out, this is the\narea of third degree burn,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 3298590,
    "dDurationMs": 2850,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "so your skin gets molten."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 3301440,
    "dDurationMs": 2460,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- Bro, you're having way\ntoo much fun with this."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 3303900,
    "dDurationMs": 1140,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- Can I ask this question?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 3305040,
    "dDurationMs": 2760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Like, do we have an eighth of a gram"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 3307800,
    "dDurationMs": 2130,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of antimatter available for this?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 3309930,
    "dDurationMs": 930,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Asking for a friend."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 3310860,
    "dDurationMs": 2730,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- Can you really steal an\neighth of a gram from CERN?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 3313590,
    "dDurationMs": 1472,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- That's a good question."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 3315062,
    "dDurationMs": 3208,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Do you know how much\nantimatter you've made in total"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 3318270,
    "dDurationMs": 900,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "in this factory?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 3319170,
    "dDurationMs": 1950,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- We make in the order of 10"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 3321120,
    "dDurationMs": 3520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to the 10 protons, antiprotons per year."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 3324640,
    "dDurationMs": 1790,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Now we can make an estimate."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 3326430,
    "dDurationMs": 3068,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This facility is around since 25 years."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 3329498,
    "dDurationMs": 5000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So let's say this is 10 to the 11 protons."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 3334500,
    "dDurationMs": 4980,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "A gram would be 10 to the 23."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 3339480,
    "dDurationMs": 3360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So we are talking here of, well,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 3342840,
    "dDurationMs": 2580,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "I'm not very good at math but it's like..."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 3345420,
    "dDurationMs": 2610,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- A trillionth of a gram."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 3348030,
    "dDurationMs": 1920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "That means that to make\none eighth of a gram"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 3349950,
    "dDurationMs": 2742,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of antimatter, the factory\nwould have to run for longer"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 3352692,
    "dDurationMs": 2418,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "than the age of the universe."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 3355110,
    "dDurationMs": 2659,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "In fact, if you took all\nthe 10 billion antiprotons"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 3357769,
    "dDurationMs": 3791,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "they make in a year and\nannihilated them all at once,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 3361560,
    "dDurationMs": 2970,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "you would produce enough\nenergy to heat one milliliter"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 3364530,
    "dDurationMs": 3123,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of water by about one degree Celsius."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 3368850,
    "dDurationMs": 4290,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- I'd love to see Croatia,\nagain, just for size and scale."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 3373140,
    "dDurationMs": 1920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- How much?\n- You tell me."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 3375060,
    "dDurationMs": 2490,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- All right. 10 grams of antimatter."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 3377550,
    "dDurationMs": 1710,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- Sure, let's do it."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 3379260,
    "dDurationMs": 833,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- Oh my God."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 3382320,
    "dDurationMs": 2820,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So while 10 grams of\nantimatter would destroy"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 3385140,
    "dDurationMs": 1500,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "an entire city..."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 3386640,
    "dDurationMs": 1740,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- Bye bye hometown."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 3388380,
    "dDurationMs": 1800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- The amounts of antimatter they're making"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 3390180,
    "dDurationMs": 2700,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "at CERN are in no way dangerous,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 3392880,
    "dDurationMs": 2290,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "which is also part of the\nreason we had some fun"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 3395170,
    "dDurationMs": 1850,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "with this simulation."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 3397020,
    "dDurationMs": 2160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Because for the far foreseeable future,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 3399180,
    "dDurationMs": 1890,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "it's just not realistic to talk"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 3401070,
    "dDurationMs": 3240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "about having macroscopic\namounts of antimatter."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 3404310,
    "dDurationMs": 1500,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So if people want to\nplay around with this,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 3405810,
    "dDurationMs": 1800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "we'll put a link in the description."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 3409380,
    "dDurationMs": 1353,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Yeah, have fun."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 3411960,
    "dDurationMs": 2252,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Or if you'd rather get\nsome antimatter yourself"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 3414212,
    "dDurationMs": 2218,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "without having to rob CERN,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 3416430,
    "dDurationMs": 1650,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "then I'll tell you how to get some."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 3418080,
    "dDurationMs": 5000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Just go to your local supermarket\nand buy yourself this."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 3423090,
    "dDurationMs": 2250,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Some bananas."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 3425340,
    "dDurationMs": 2370,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "That's because a banana\ncontains trace amounts"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 3427710,
    "dDurationMs": 3120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of the radioactive isotope potassium-40."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 3430830,
    "dDurationMs": 2130,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And roughly every 75 minutes,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 3432960,
    "dDurationMs": 3424,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "one of these atoms decays\nand releases a positron."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 3436384,
    "dDurationMs": 2276,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Which means that if you wanted to match"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 3438660,
    "dDurationMs": 1980,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the antimatter factory's output, in terms"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 3440640,
    "dDurationMs": 3843,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of antiparticles, you would\nneed about a billion bananas."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 3447390,
    "dDurationMs": 1680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Now that's a lot of bananas,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 3449070,
    "dDurationMs": 2280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and I don't recommend eating that many."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 3451350,
    "dDurationMs": 3900,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But the thing is, even if\nyou never eat any bananas,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 3455250,
    "dDurationMs": 2580,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "odds are there are some trace amounts"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 3457830,
    "dDurationMs": 2550,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of radioactive materials inside of you."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 3460380,
    "dDurationMs": 3330,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And some of those will produce antimatter."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 3463710,
    "dDurationMs": 1350,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "One article estimates"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 3465060,
    "dDurationMs": 4454,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that the average human makes\naround 180 positrons per hour."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 3469514,
    "dDurationMs": 2956,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And so there truly is no need to be scared"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 3472470,
    "dDurationMs": 2070,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of antimatter, because you"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 3474540,
    "dDurationMs": 3453,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "have been your own little\nantimatter factory all along."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 3481650,
    "dDurationMs": 2430,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Hey, just a few final things."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 3484080,
    "dDurationMs": 2310,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The first thing is I want\nto give a big shout out"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 3486390,
    "dDurationMs": 2430,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to Physics Girl, who made an amazing video"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 3488820,
    "dDurationMs": 2400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "for the antimatter factory years ago."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 3491220,
    "dDurationMs": 1980,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And ever since I watched that video,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 3493200,
    "dDurationMs": 1380,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "I've always wanted to go."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 3494580,
    "dDurationMs": 1950,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So it's been a huge inspiration,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 3496530,
    "dDurationMs": 3270,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and I highly recommend you\ncheck out that video here."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 3499800,
    "dDurationMs": 2280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The other thing is I want\nto give a quick shout out"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 3502080,
    "dDurationMs": 1320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to all the people at CERN,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 3503400,
    "dDurationMs": 2670,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "those who helped us\nwith all the animations,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 3506070,
    "dDurationMs": 2095,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "those who've hosted us and\ntaken the time to explain"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 3508165,
    "dDurationMs": 3995,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "their live work, and everyone\nelse, thank you so much."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 3512160,
    "dDurationMs": 2430,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And the third and final\nthank you is of course,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 3514590,
    "dDurationMs": 1680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "as always, to you."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 3516270,
    "dDurationMs": 1590,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Thank you so much for watching,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 3517860,
    "dDurationMs": 2433,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and I'm excited to see\nyou at the next one."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 3528330,
    "dDurationMs": 1983,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "AntiCasper, Casper, annihilate."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 3532320,
    "dDurationMs": 1113,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "All right, that's it."
    } ]
  } ]
}
